\h Yehoshua
\toc1 Yehoshua
\toc2 Yehoshua
\toc3 Yehoshua
\mt1 Yehoshua
\mt2 (Joshua)
\is1 Introduction
\ip This account about Yehoshua, traditionally ‘Joshua’ in English (after ‘I’ and then ‘J’ changed over the centuries from a ‘Y’ sound), tells how the Israelis invaded Canaan and took control of the land. Yehoshua led them forward now after replacing Mosheh (Moses) when he passed away somewhere on a mountain. Some of the main events described in this document include: their crossing the Yordan river, the demolition of Yeriho (traditionally ‘Jericho’), the war at Ay, the allocation of blocks of land to the various Israeli tribes and others, and the renewal of the agreement between God and his people.
\ip The most well-known saying in this account is, “…choose for yourselves today who you will serve… But as for me and my household, we will serve Yahweh.” (24:15).
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 The defeat of the Canaanites \ior 1:1–12:24\ior*
\io1 The division of land \ior 13:1–21:45\ior*
\io2 a. The land east of the River Yordan \ior 13:1-33\ior*
\io2 b. The land west of the River Yordan \ior 14:1–19:51\ior*
\io2 c. The refuge cities \ior 20:1-9\ior*
\io2 d. The cities for Levites \ior 21:1-45\ior*
\io1 The returning home of some tribes back to the east of the Yordan \ior 22:1-34\ior*
\io1 Yehoshua's final instructions \ior 23:1-16\ior*
\io1 The renewal of the agreement there at Shikim \ior 24:1-33\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 Yahweh encourages Yehoshua
\rem /s1 God Commands Joshua to Conquer Canaan; God's Commission to Joshua; The Lord Commands Joshua; The Lord's Charge to Joshua; Prelude to the conquest of Canaan
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 After¦99058 the death¦99059 of Yahweh's¦99062 servant Mosheh \add !(Moses¦99060)\add*, Yahweh spoke¦99063 to¦99065 Mosheh's¦99072 servant Yehoshua¦99067 \add !(Joshua¦99067)\add* (the son¦99068 of Nun¦99070), saying¦99063,
\v 2 “Now¦99078 that my¦99076 servant¦99076 Mosheh¦99075 is dead, you¦99085 and all¦99086 \add #these\add* people¦99088 \add ≈should pack up\add* \add and\add* cross¦99080 over¦99080 this¦99084 \add River\add* Yordan¦99083 \add to go\add* to the¦99088 land¦99092 that I¦99094 am¦99095 about¦99095 to give¦99095 to them—to Yisra'el's¦99098 descendants.
\v 3 I'll give¦99110 you¦99109 all every place¦99102 that¦99103 the¦99105 \add #soles¦99105\add* of¦99100 your¦99107 \add #feet¦99107\add* tread¦99104 on¦99108, just¦99111 like I told Mosheh¦99115.\x + \xo 1:3-5: \xt Deu 11:24-25.\x*
\v 4 Your \add ≈territory¦99137 will¦99136 extend\add* from the wilderness¦99117 \add in the south\add* to the Lebanon¦99118 \add mountains in the north\add*, and from the large¦99123 Euphrates¦99126 River¦99124 \add in the east\add*, and \add ≈right to the Mediterranean\add* sea¦99132 \add ≈in the west\add*, including¦99118 all¦99127 of¦99134 the Hittites' land¦99128.
\v 5 No man will¦99141 \add ≈be able to¦99143 challenge your¦99143 leadership as long as you live\add*—I'll¦99152 be with you just¦99147 as I was¦99148 with Mosheh¦99151—I won't¦99154 fail you or abandon¦99157 you.\x + \xo 1:5: \xt Deu 31:6,8; Heb 13:5.\x*
\v 6 Be¦99160 strong¦99159 and¦99160 be¦99160 courageous¦99160, for¦99161 you¦99162 yourself will¦99163 \add ≈lead\add* \add #these\add* people¦99166 to inherit¦99163 the¦99166 land¦99170 that I promised their¦99174 ancestors¦99174 that I'd give¦99175 to them.\x + \xo 1:6: \xt Deu 31:6-7,23.\x*
\v 7 Just be strong¦99179 and¦99180 very¦99181 courageous¦99180—making sure that you \add ≈obey everything\add* that my¦99190 servant¦99190 Mosheh¦99189 instructed¦99188 you. Don't¦99191 turn¦99193 away to the right¦99195 or to the left¦99196 from¦99194 it¦99194, so¦99197 that you'll¦99201 be wise in every¦99199 \add ≈situation¦99187 that you end¦99187 up¦99187 in\add*.
\v 8 That¦99225 book¦99206 of¦99206 the¦99206 law¦99207 \add ^must always be on your lips\add* and you should¦99215 meditate¦99210 on it day¦99212 and night¦99213, so¦99214 that you'll be careful to¦99217 follow everything¦99217 that's¦99214 written¦99219 in¦99220 it, because¦99221 then you'll make¦99224 your ways¦99227 prosperous and then you'll be wise.
\v 9 Didn't I¦99232 order you to be strong¦99233 and¦99234 courageous¦99234? Don't¦99231 tremble or be discouraged¦99240 because¦99241 your¦99244 god¦99244 Yahweh¦99243 will¦99247 be with¦99245 you wherever¦99246 you go¦99247.”
\s1 Yehoshua instructs the people
