\v 4 \add ≈However, Rahab had hidden¦99531\add* the two¦99529 men \add ≈so she¦99531 answered¦99532\add*, “Indeed, the men \add ≈arrived¦99535 here, but¦99525\add* I¦99539 didn't¦99538 know¦99539 where¦99540 they¦99541 were¦99541 from¦99540.
\v 5 \add ≈But¦99543 as\add* the \add city\add* gate¦99544 was¦99545 \add ≈about¦99545\add* to shut¦99545 \add ≈last night\add*, the men¦99547 went out¦99548. I¦99550 don't¦99549 know¦99550 to where¦99551 \add *they¦99552\add* went—if you all hurry, you might be able to \add ≈catch\add* them¦99556.”
\v 6 (\add ≈But¦99560 actually\add* she¦99560 had¦99561 taken¦99561 them up¦99561 onto her¦99567 \add flat\add* roof¦99562 and¦99560 hidden¦99563 them in¦99564 \add ≈bundles of¦99564 flax that¦99566 were¦99566 drying there\add*.)
\v 7 \add ≈So¦99576\add* the \add ≈guards hurried\add* out¦99583 on the road¦99575 to¦99577 the fords¦99578 on the Yordan¦99576 \add River\add* and¦99579 the \add city\add* gate¦99579 was kept shut after¦99585 \add *they¦99573\add* had¦99583 left.
