\v 8 Before the Israeli men lay¦99589 down¦99589 \add to sleep that night\add*, \add @Rahab¦99587\add* went¦99591 up¦99591 them¦99592 on¦99593 the roof¦99595
\v 9 and told \add *them\add*, “\add #We\add* know¦99601 that Yahweh¦99605 has¦99604 given¦99604 this land¦99609 to¦99598 you all and we're \add ≈all terrified\add* of you. Everyone¦99601 that lives here is \add ≈trembling at the¦99619 thought of your¦99613 coming\add*
\v 10 because¦99623 we've¦99624 heard that¦99639 Yahweh¦99629 dried¦99628 up¦99628 the water¦99632 of the Red Sea¦99633 ahead¦99636 of you all when¦99637 you left¦99637 Egypt¦99638 \add !(Mitsrayim¦99638)\add*. And¦99638 \add ≡we heard\add* what you all did¦99640 to¦99641 two¦99641 of the Amorite¦99643 kings¦99642 Sihon¦99647 and¦99648 Og¦99648 over the Yordan¦99646 there—how you all completely destroyed¦99650 them.\x + \xo 2:10: a \xt Exo 14:21; \xo b \xt Num 21:21-35.\x*
\v 11 \add ≈Yes,\add* we've heard¦99653 \add <the reports\add* and \add ≈we trembled and lost our¦99655 courage to fight you¦99662 all\add* because¦99662 your¦99665 god¦99665 Yahweh¦99664, he's¦99666 God¦99665 \add ≈over\add* the heavens¦99668 above¦99669 and the earth¦99672 below¦99673.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦99675\add* now¦99675, please¦99678 promise me by¦99680 Yahweh¦99680 that because¦99681 I've¦99683 been kind to¦99696 \add both of\add* you, you all will¦99695 act kindly towards my father's¦99693 household¦99692. Give¦99695 me \add ≈a¦99697 guarantee that you'll do¦99686 what you promise\add*
\v 13 and spare¦99700 my parents¦99706 and my siblings and their families from¦99723 death¦99723.”
\p
\v 14 “Our¦99728 lives \add ≈for¦99726 your lives\add*,” the¦99727 \add two\add* men¦99727 agreed. “If¦99731 you don't¦99732 tell¦99733 \add ≈anyone about¦99728 our¦99736 agreement\add*, then¦99725 when¦99739 Yahweh¦99741 gives¦99739 us¦99742 this¦99737 land¦99745, we'll¦99746 \add ≈show\add* kindness and¦99725 faithfulness¦99749 to¦99726 you.”
