\v 22 \add @The¦99882 two men\add* went¦99881 up into the hills and stayed there¦99884 for three¦99885 days¦99886 until¦99887 the search¦99891 party returned¦99889 \add to the city\add* after searching all¦99893 the roads and not¦99896 finding¦99897 them¦99897.
\v 23 \add ≈So¦99899\add* the two¦99900 men¦99901 went¦99902 down¦99902 to the river and crossed¦99904 over¦99904 and returned¦99899 to Yehoshua¦99908 (Nun's¦99911 son¦99909), and they¦99905 told him¦99914 everything that¦99918 had¦99918 happened¦99918.
\v 24 “Yahweh¦99928 has¦99927 certainly given¦99927 this land¦99934 to us,” they told Yehoshua¦99924. “The¦99940 people there won't be able to resist us because¦99942 they're so terrified.”
\c 3
\s1 The Israelis cross the Yordan
