\p
\v 1 Early¦99945 the next morning¦99947, Yehoshua¦99946 \add and the people\add* got up early¦99945 and set¦99948 off from¦99949 Acacia Grove and went¦99950 as far as the Yordan¦99953 \add River\add* and camped¦99959 there¦99960 without crossing over¦99962.
\v 2 After three¦99966 days¦99967, the leaders went¦99968 throughout the camp¦99971
\v 3 and instructed¦99973 the people¦99976, “As¦99978 soon as¦99978 you all see the box¦99980 \add containing\add* the agreement¦99981 with your god¦99984 Yahweh¦99983, and \add ≡see\add* the Levitical¦99986 priests¦99985 carrying¦99987 it, then¦99973 you yourselves should move out¦99990 from¦99991 your places¦99991 and follow after¦99993 it.
\v 4 But¦100000 keep about¦100002 nine hundred metres back from¦100024 it¦99998. Don't¦100005 go any closer than that so¦100009 that you all can see the¦100015 way to¦100008 go, because¦100020 \add ≈we haven't been¦99998 this way\add* before.”
\p
\v 5 Then Yehoshua¦100029 told the people¦100032, “\add ≈Make sure you¦100038 all do the ritual washing to¦100030 make yourselves¦100033 pure\add*, because¦100034 tomorrow¦100035 Yahweh¦100037 will¦100036 do miracles¦100039 among us.”
\v 6 And¦100042 \add *he¦100041\add* told the priests¦100045, “Lift¦100047 up the box¦100050 with the agreement¦100051, and \add ≈walk across here in front\add* of the people.” \add ≈So¦100041\add* they¦100055 lifted¦100055 up the \add sacred\add* chest¦100050 and went¦100060 \add ≈and stood in front of all\add* the people.
\p
\v 7 Then Yahweh¦100066 told Yehoshua¦100069, “Today I'll¦100072 begin¦100072 to¦100067 make¦100073 you powerful in¦100074 the¦100070 eyes¦100074 of¦100074 all¦100075 Yisrael¦100077 \add !(Israel¦100077)\add* so they'll¦100079 know¦100079 that¦100071 I'm with you just¦100081 like I was¦100082 with Mosheh¦100085.
\v 8 Tell the priests¦100093 who¦100094 are carrying¦100094 the \add sacred\add* chest¦100095 that as soon as they come¦100099 to¦100100 the edge¦100102 of¦100102 the river, they should \add ≈go in¦100105 just¦100099 a little and¦100089 then¦100089 stop there\add*.”
\p
\v 9 Then Yehoshua¦100110 told the¦100113 Israelis¦100114, “\add ≈Gather around\add* here and¦100117 listen¦100117 to¦100111 your¦100122 god¦100122 Yahweh's¦100121 message¦100120.”
\v 10 \add *He¦100124\add* told \add <them\add*, “This¦100126 is how you'll all know¦100127 that¦100126 God¦100129, who can do anything, is among you. With¦100125 your¦100131 own eyes, you'll all see how he'll¦100133 take away the land from¦100134 the Canaanites¦100137, the Hittites¦100140, the Hivites¦100143, the Perizzites¦100146, the Girgashites¦100149, the Amorites¦100150, and¦100124 the Yebusites¦100151.
\v 11 Listen, the sacred chest¦100154 containing the slabs that belongs to the master¦100156 who \add owns\add* the whole¦100157 world, is¦100160 about¦100160 to \add be taken\add* across the Yordan¦100162 in¦100162 front¦100161 of¦100154 you¦100161.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦100171\add* now¦100164, \add ≈select one¦100174 man¦100169 from¦100170 each of¦100170 your twelve tribes¦100170\add*,
\v 13 and¦100180 as soon as the \add ≈priests¦100184 carrying¦100185 the sacred chest¦100186 go into the Yordan¦100193, as soon as their feet¦100183 touch the water, the river water on¦100192 the upstream side\add* will¦100198 pile up in¦100192 a heap¦100201.”
\p
\v 14 \add ≈So¦100204 once the people¦100206 had packed up their¦100207 tents¦100207 ready to¦100208 cross¦100208 the river\add*, the priests¦100212 carrying¦100213 the sacred box¦100214 walked ahead in¦100205 front¦100216 of¦100216 them.
\v 15 Then¦100219 as soon as \add ≈those¦100220 priests¦100226\add* steeped into the \add edge\add* of¦100225 the \add ≈fast-flowing\add* river (because it¦100233 overflowed its¦100238 banks¦100238 at¦100230 harvest¦100241 time¦100240 \add in the spring\add*),
\v 16 then¦100243 the water coming¦100245 from¦100246 upstream \add suddenly\add* stopped flowing. The¦100244 water far¦100251 upstream piled up near a town¦100255 called Adam¦100253 (near Tsaretan), and¦100243 the water that¦100256 normally flowed down¦100259 towards the Sea of¦100261 Aravah¦100262 (\add also called\add* the Dead Sea or the Salt¦100265 Sea) \add ≈stopped flowing\add*, so the people¦100268 were¦100266 able to¦100246 cross \add what was\add* the Yordan River opposite Yeriho¦100271 \add !(Jericho¦100271)\add*.
\v 17 The¦100274 priests¦100274 carrying¦100275 the sacred chest¦100276 with¦100280 Yahweh's¦100279 agreement¦100277 \add in it\add*, stood¦100273 on firm, dry ground in \add what had been\add* the middle¦100281 of¦100282 the river. All¦100284 the Israelis¦100286 crossed¦100296 over¦100287 on dry ground until¦100289 everyone¦100284 was across.
\c 4
\s1 The memorial of boulders
\rem /s1 Twelve Stones Set Up at Gilgal; Memorial Stones Are Set Up; Memorials to the Jordan Crossing
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Once all¦100305 the people had¦100304 crossed¦100308 over¦100308 the Yordan¦100311 River, Yahweh¦100314 told Yehoshua¦100317,
\v 2 “Take¦100320 \add those\add* twelve men¦100327 \add ≈that the¦100324 people¦100324 selected from¦100334 each tribe¦100334\add*,
\v 3 and give them these instructions: Pick up¦100339 twelve boulders¦100352 from here¦100342 in the middle¦100343 of¦100343 the Yordan¦100344 from near where the priests¦100347 are standing¦100345, and bring them over¦100353 with¦100358 you, and put them in the place¦100358 where you all camp tonight.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦100376\add* Yehoshua¦100367 called¦100366 \add over\add* the¦100371 twelve men, one¦100379 from¦100383 each tribe¦100383,
\v 5 and told them¦100386, “Cross¦100387 \add ≈back to where\add* your god¦100392 Yahweh's¦100391 box¦100390 is in¦100389 the middle¦100395 of the Yordan¦100396 and \add ≈each of you¦100398 should pick up¦100397 a rock¦100400 and carry it¦100385 back on your\add* shoulder—one stone¦100400 each on your shoulder to match the number¦100405 of tribes¦100406 of Yisra'el's¦100409 sons.
\v 6 \add ≈Those boulders will¦100423 be¦100412 a¦100414 monument for¦100416 all the people\add*. \add ≈In¦100415 the future when your¦100419 children¦100419 ask¦100418 what¦100422 those¦100424 boulders mean\add*,
\v 7 then¦100427 you'll all be¦100443 able to¦100428 tell them¦100428 that the water in the Yordan¦100432 River was cut¦100440 off¦100440 ahead of¦100434 the box¦100434 with¦100438 Yahweh's¦100437 agreement¦100435. When¦100427 it¦100438 crossed¦100438 over into¦100446 the river, the water in the river \add ≈stopped flowing\add*, and¦100443 those¦100445 boulders¦100444 are a memorial¦100446 for¦100447 the Israelis¦100448 forever¦100451.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦100453\add* the Israelis¦100458 did just what Yehoshua had told¦100461 them to do, and they¦100463 picked up¦100463 twelve boulders¦100467 from¦100468 the Yordan¦100469, just as¦100470 Yahweh¦100472 had instructed¦100461 Yehoshua, and brought them over¦100481 to where \add the people\add* were camping and placed¦100485 them down¦100486 there¦100487.
\v 9 Then¦100489 Yehoshua¦100493 stacked up¦100492 twelve other boulders¦100491 in¦100494 the middle¦100494 of the Yordan¦100495 where the feet¦100498 of the priests¦100499 carrying¦100500 the box¦100501 with the agreement¦100502 had been¦100503, and¦100503 they¦100503 remain there¦100504 until¦100505 today.
\v 10 The¦100509 priests¦100509 carrying¦100510 the box¦100511 had stood¦100512 in¦100513 the middle¦100513 of¦100514 the Yordan¦100514 until¦100515 everything¦100517 that¦100520 Yahweh¦100523 had instructed Yehoshua to pass¦100541 on to the people was¦100516 done, just as Mosheh¦100535 had \add also\add* instructed Yehoshua, and¦100509 the people had rapidly crossed¦100541 over¦100541.
\p
\v 11 As¦100544 soon as¦100544 all¦100547 the people had¦100546 crossed over, the priests¦100555 carrying Yahweh's¦100554 box¦100552 \add also\add* crossed over in¦100556 front¦100556 of¦100556 the people.
\v 12 The¦100572 \add soldiers\add* from the tribes¦100567 of Reuben¦100562, and Gad¦100565 and the half-tribe of Menashsheh¦100568 had \add ≈marched\add* over¦100559 ahead of the rest of the Israeli¦100571, as¦100573 Mosheh¦100576 had \add ≈agreed with them¦100575\add*.
\v 13 (\add There were\add* around forty¦100578 thousand¦100579 of them, armed and ready for battle, and they¦100582 were heading to¦100586 the plains¦100587 of Yeriho¦100588 \add !(Jericho¦100588)\add* for the battle \add there\add*.)
\v 14 On¦100601 that¦100592 day¦100591, Yahweh¦100594 helped Yehoshua¦100597 to look powerful in¦100598 the eyes¦100598 of the people, and¦100602 they respected him¦100603 just¦100604 as¦100604 they had¦100605 respected Mosheh¦100608 all¦100609 the days¦100611 of his\f + \fr 4:14 \ft The Hebrew doesn't make it clear here whether the writer meant all of \+bd Mosheh's life\+bd* or all of \+bd Yehoshua's life\+bd*, so translations will vary.\f* life¦100612.
\p
\v 15 Then Yahweh¦100616 told Yehoshua¦100619,
\v 16 “\add ≈Now order\add* the priests¦100625 carrying¦100626 the box¦100627 with the agreement to come¦100629 up¦100629 out of¦100626 \add what was\add* the Yordan¦100632 \add River\add*,”
