\p
\v 19 The¦100677 people¦100677 had come up¦100678 from¦100679 the river valley \add ≈around the end of March¦100681\add* and¦100685 they¦100678 camped¦100685 east¦100688 of Yeriho¦100689 \add !(Jericho¦100689)\add* at¦100682 Gilgal¦100686,
\v 20 which¦100696 was where \add #they¦100697\add* had¦100697 set¦100701 up¦100701 the¦100694 \add monument of\add* twelve boulders¦100694.
\v 21 Then¦100705 \add @Yehoshua¦100712\add* told the Israelis¦100709, “\add ≈In¦100715 the future\add* when your¦100713 descendants ask¦100712 why these¦100721 boulders¦100720 are¦100720 here,
\v 22 tell them that¦100734 this¦100734 is where Yisrael¦100730 crossed the¦100733 Yordan¦100733 \add River\add* on¦100728 dry land.
\v 23 Your¦100745 god¦100740 Yahweh¦100739 dried up the river water¦100743 ahead¦100745 of¦100743 you until¦100746 you'd all crossed over, just¦100749 as¦100749 \add *he\add* had¦100748 done¦100750 when he dried up the Red Sea¦100753 before¦100759 we¦100762 crossed over.
\v 24 Yahweh¦100773 did that so that all the peoples¦100768 in the world would know¦100765 that he is¦100775 powerful, \add and\add* so that you'll always all respect him.
\c 5
\rem /s1 The New Generation Circumcised; Circumcision at Gilgal
\p
\v 1 When all the Amorite¦100793 kings who¦100794 were¦100795 on¦100795 the \add west\add* side¦100795 of¦100795 the Yordan (towards the ocean) and all the Canaanite¦100801 kings (beside the ocean) heard¦100789 how¦100807 Yahweh¦100810 had dried¦100809 up¦100809 the water¦100813 in¦100795 the Yordan \add River\add* until¦100819 \add @the Israelis¦100818\add* had crossed¦100821 over¦100821, they¦100821 \add ≈trembled with¦100795 fear\add* and \add ≈lost their¦100824 nerve to¦100797 stand against\add* Yisrael¦100818.
\s1 Circumcising the males and celebrating ‘pass-over’ at Gilgal
