\p
\v 2 At¦100837 that¦100838 time¦100837, Yahweh¦100840 told Yehoshua¦100843, “Make¦100844 yourself¦100845 flint¦100847 knives¦100846 and¦100848 again¦100848 circumcise¦100849 the¦100852 male Israelis¦100854.”
\v 3 So¦100857 Yehoshua¦100860 \add had\add* flint¦100862 knives¦100861 made¦100857 and¦100863 the¦100866 \add male\add* Israelis¦100867 were circumcised¦100863 at \add a place they named\add* ‘The¦100870 hill¦100870 of¦100870 foreskins¦100871’.
\v 4 (This¦100873 was done because all¦100879 the men¦100887 who'd left¦100882 Egypt¦100883 and¦100873 who were old enough to join the army \add had been circumcised but\add* had died¦100889 in¦100890 the wilderness¦100890 since then¦100873,\x + \xo 5:6: \xt Num 14:28-35.\x*
\v 5 \add and\add* because¦100895 all¦100903 the \add ≈boys\add* who'd been born¦100906 while they were in¦100907 the wilderness¦100907 after they'd left¦100902 Egypt¦100910 hadn't been circumcised¦100897.
\v 6 The¦100920 Israelis¦100922 had spent forty¦100917 years¦100918 \add ≈moving\add* around the wilderness¦100923 until¦100924 the last of¦100930 those men¦100930 who'd left¦100932 Egypt¦100933 but¦100958 hadn't listened¦100937 to Yahweh \add ≈had died\add*. Yahweh had promised not¦100935 to let¦100945 them see¦100945 the land that¦100949 \add *he'd¦100951\add* promised to their¦100952 ancestors¦100952 to give¦100953 them—a land flowing¦100956 with¦100923 milk¦100957 and¦100958 honey¦100958.
\v 7 It was the sons of¦100962 those¦100964 people¦100975 that Yehoshua¦100967 had¦100975 circumcised \add this time\add* because¦100968 they¦100971 hadn't been circumcised on¦100977 the way¦100977.)
\p
\v 8 After all¦100983 their¦100988 males had¦100982 been circumcised¦100986, they remained in¦100989 that camp¦100989 until¦100990 they'd \add ≈healed¦100991 up\add*.
\v 9 Then Yahweh¦100995 told Yehoshua¦100998, “Today I've¦101000 rolled¦101000 away¦101000 the¦101003 disgrace of¦101003 Egypt¦101004 from¦101005 you,” and¦101006 that¦101013 place¦101008 is named Gilgal¦101010\f + \fr 5:9 \ft The name ‘Gilgal’ (‘גִּלְגָּל’, ‘circle’) sounds like ‘galal’ (‘גַּלַל’, ‘roll’).\f* until¦101011 this¦101013 day¦100999.
