\p
\v 13 While Yehoshua was in the Yeriho¦101067 \add !(Jericho¦101067) area\add*, he¦101068 looked up¦101068 and saw¦101070 a man in front¦101075 of¦101069 him. The man had drawn¦101077 his sword¦101076 and was holding it¦101064 in his hand¦101078 \add ≈so\add* Yehoshua approached him and asked, “Are¦101085 you¦101085 on¦101065 \em our\em* side, or¦101086 with¦101065 our enemies?”
\p
\v 14 “No¦101092,” the man \add ≈answered¦101090\add*, “but¦101090 I¦101094, the leader of¦101097 Yahweh's¦101099 army¦101097, have¦101101 come¦101101 now¦101100.”
\p Then¦101090 Yehoshua¦101103 fell¦101102 \add ≈to his knees\add* and bowed¦101108 down¦101108 with his face¦101106 to the¦101095 ground, and \add ≈asked¦101113\add* him¦101110, “What's¦101111 my¦101112 master¦101112 going to \add ≈command¦101095\add* to his servant¦101116?”
\p
\v 15 “Take¦101126 off your¦101128 sandals¦101128,” the commander¦101119 of¦101121 Yahweh's¦101122 army¦101121 told \add *him¦101136\add*, “because¦101131 the ground that¦101133 you're¦101134 standing¦101135 is¦101137 holy¦101137.” \add ≈So¦101118\add* Yehoshua¦101125 \add ≈took¦101126 them off\add*.
\c 6
\s1 Yeriho's walls collapse
\rem /s1 Jericho Taken and Destroyed; The Fall of Jericho
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now¦101143\add* Yeriho¦101143 \add !(Jericho¦101143) city\add* was shut-up tightly \add ≈because of¦101146 the¦101147 Israelis¦101148\add*, \add so\add* no one was coming¦101152 out¦101150 and¦101143 no one could go¦101150 in¦101146.
\v 2 Then Yahweh¦101156 told Yehoshua¦101159, “Listen, I've¦101161 given¦101161 you \add ≈victory over\add* Yeriho¦101165 and its¦101168 king¦101168, and \add ≈their\add* mighty¦101169 army \add >warriors\add*.
\v 3 All¦101176 your soldiers must¦101172 go¦101172 around¦101172 the¦101175 city¦101182 once every day¦101188 for six¦101187 days¦101188
\v 4 with¦101198 seven priests \add ≈blowing\add* ram's horns going ahead of¦101196 the sacred box¦101197. On¦101201 the seventh¦101199 day¦101198, you all must¦101192 go¦101200 around the city¦101203 seven times¦101205 while the priests are blowing the horns.
\v 5 \add ≈Finally¦101217,\add* with¦101211 a long blast¦101211 of¦101213 the horn¦101214, when¦101211 you all hear¦101215 that then¦101210 all the people¦101224 must¦101221 shout¦101225 loudly¦101226 and the wall¦101228 around¦101230 the city¦101229 will¦101231 fall¦101227 down flat, and all the \add ≈soldiers\add* should go¦101231 straight¦101234 in¦101211 \add from where they're standing\add*.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦101236\add* Yehoshua¦101237 summoned the priests and told them¦101245, “Carry¦101240 the box with the agreement¦101250, and have seven priests hold up¦101246 seven rams' horns¦101256 \add ≈ahead\add* of¦101257 Yahweh's¦101259 box.”
\v 7 Then¦101261 he¦101261 told the people¦101265, “Go¦101268 across in¦101273 front¦101273 and¦101261 go¦101267 around¦101267 the city¦101270, \add ≈with the soldiers going ahead\add* of¦101273 Yahweh's¦101275 box¦101274.”
\p
\v 8 After¦101296 Yehoshua¦101279 had¦101278 spoken¦101278 to¦101280 the people¦101282, the seven priests¦101284 with their seven rams' horns went¦101297 across in¦101293 front¦101289 and blew the horns, and the box¦101294 with Yahweh's¦101290 covenant¦101295 was¦101297 \add ≈carried¦101285\add* along behind¦101298 them¦101298.
\v 9 The¦101300 \add ≈soldiers\add* walked ahead of¦101302 the priests¦101303 blowing the horns, with¦101313 the rear guard¦101307 walking behind¦101309 the box¦101310. \add So\add* they were¦101304 walking and¦101300 blowing the horns,
\v 10 and¦101315 Yehoshua¦101319 told¦101318 the people¦101317, “Don't¦101321 shout \add ≈or even speak or make¦101325 a¦101333 noise\add* until¦101334 the day¦101335 I¦101336 tell you all to¦101337 shout—then¦101315 you all should shout loudly.”
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦101341\add* Yahweh's¦101344 box¦101342 was carried once around¦101341 the city¦101347, then¦101341 the people went¦101341 back to¦101341 the camp¦101352 and¦101341 stayed¦101353 the night¦101353 there.
\p
\v 12 Yehoshua¦101358 got up early¦101357 the next morning¦101359, and¦101357 the priests¦101361 picked up Yahweh's¦101365 box¦101364
\v 13 and the seven priests¦101368 holding the seven rams' horns went in front of \add *it\add*—blowing¦101378 the horns as they¦101378 kept walking. The¦101387 \add ≈soldiers\add* walking in front of them¦101382, and the rear guard¦101383 walked behind¦101385 Yahweh's¦101375 box¦101374 \add ≈while\add* the horns were¦101369 being blown.
\v 14 They¦101394 went¦101393 once around¦101393 the¦101396 city¦101396 on that second¦101398 day¦101397 and¦101401 then¦101393 returned¦101401 to their camp¦101402 \add again\add*—doing¦101404 that for six¦101405 days¦101406.
\p
\v 15 Then¦101408 on the seventh¦101411 day they got up¦101413 early¦101412 at dawn¦101414 and¦101408 went around the city¦101418 \add ≈as¦101413 before\add*, except this¦101420 day they went around seven¦101430 times¦101431.
\v 16 \add ≈After that seventh¦101435 time¦101434 around,\add* the priests¦101437 blew \add a long blast\add* on¦101434 the rams' horns and¦101439 Yehoshua¦101440 told the people¦101443, “Shout¦101444, because¦101445 Yahweh¦101448 has¦101447 given¦101447 you¦101449 all the city¦101452!
\v 17 \add However,\add* everything in the city¦101455 is¦101462 sacred to Yahweh¦101463. Only¦101464 the prostitute¦101466 Rahab¦101465 and¦101454 those who¦101471 are in her¦101472 house¦101473 will¦101467 be¦101454 allowed to live¦101467, because¦101474 she¦101475 hid¦101475 the spies that¦101471 we¦101480 sent¦101480 in.
\v 18 But¦101482 for all of you, everything inside the city is forbidden—if any¦101493 of you take¦101492 anything out of the city then our camp¦101499 \add ≈would also¦101492 then be marked for destruction¦101491\add* and¦101482 it¦101503 would cause \add a lot of\add* trouble¦101502.
\v 19 All¦101514 the¦101515 silver¦101507 and gold¦101508, bronze¦101510 and iron¦101511 is¦101512 dedicated to¦101514 Yahweh¦101516 and must¦101517 go¦101517 into \add *his\add* treasury¦101515.
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦101519\add* the people shouted¦101532 when that horn blew—as soon as they heard¦101524 \add *it¦101523\add* the people shouted loudly¦101533 and the wall¦101535 fell¦101534 down on¦101522 itself and the people went up \add and over\add* into the city from wherever they were¦101523 standing and captured¦101542 the city.\x + \xo 6:20: \xt Heb 11:30.\x*
\v 21 They¦101548 \add ≈killed\add* every \add living thing\add* in¦101553 the¦101566 city¦101553 with¦101553 their \add #swords¦101568\add*, including¦101555 men and women¦101557, young¦101558 and old¦101561, even cattle, sheep¦101564, and donkeys¦101565.
\p
\v 22 Then¦101570 Yehoshua¦101577 commanded the two¦101570 men¦101571 who had¦101572 spied¦101572 on the area, “Go¦101578 to the prostitute's¦101582 house¦101579 and bring¦101583 the woman¦101587 out¦101572 of¦101590 it¦101594 and all who are related to her, just¦101595 as¦101595 you promised her.”
\v 23 \add ≈So¦101599\add* the young¦101600 men¦101600 \add ≈who'd gone in as\add* spies¦101601 went¦101599 in and brought¦101602 out¦101602 Rahab¦101605 and her parents¦101611 and all¦101623 her relatives and settled them¦101627 outside¦101628 of the camp¦101629 of the Israelis¦101630.
\v 24 Then¦101632 \add @the warriors¦101633\add* set fire¦101634 to the city¦101632 and burnt¦101633 everything that¦101637 was¦101639 in¦101634 it¦101639. Only¦101640 the silver¦101642 and gold¦101643, and bronze¦101645 and iron¦101646 were \add first removed and\add* put¦101647 into the treasury¦101648 of¦101649 Yahweh's¦101651 house¦101649.
\v 25 \add ≈But¦101653\add* Yehoshua spared the prostitute¦101656 Rahab¦101655 and her father's¦101660 household¦101659 and her other relatives because¦101676 she hid¦101677 the men that¦101675 Yehoshua had¦101683 sent¦101683 in to spy¦101685 on¦101671 Yeriho¦101688 \add !(Jericho¦101688)\add*, and she still lives¦101668 in Yisrael¦101672 to this¦101675 day¦101674.\x + \xo 6:25: \xt Heb 11:31.\x*
\p
\v 26 At¦101693 that¦101694 time¦101693, Yehoshua¦101692 made \add @the¦101705 people\add* take an¦101691 oath¦101691, saying¦101695,\x + \xo 6:26: \xt 1Ki 16:34.\x*
\q1 “May Yahweh¦101699 curse¦101696 anyone who¦101700 rebuilds¦101702 this¦101706 city¦101705, Yeriho¦101709 \add !(Jericho¦101709)\add*.
\q1 When that person lays its¦101714 foundation¦101711, may his¦101710 oldest son¦101712 die.
\q1 And¦101702 when he¦101702 finishes building¦101702 the city wall and¦101712 sets¦101713 up¦101713 its gates¦101714, may his youngest¦101712 son die.”
\p
\v 27 \add ≈So¦101716\add* Yahweh¦101717 was¦101716 with¦101718 Yehoshua¦101720 and¦101716 \add ≈everyone¦101723 in¦101723 that region had heard about¦101722 him¦101722\add*.
\c 7
\s1 Achan's sin
\rem /s1 Ai Defeats the Israelites; The Sin of Achan and Its Punishment; Achan's Sin
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However\add* the Israelis disobeyed the command about¦101728 \add ≈not taking anything\add*. Achan¦101734 (son of Karmi¦101737, son of Zabdi¦101740, son of Zerah¦101743, from the tribe¦101744 of Yehudah¦101745) took¦101733 something that was prohibited, \add ≈so\add* Yahweh¦101752 was angry with¦101732 the Israelis.
\p
\v 2 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Yehoshua¦101757 sent¦101756 some of his men from¦101759 Yeriho¦101759 \add !(Jericho¦101759)\add* to Ay (east¦101766 of Beyt-El and near Beyt-Aven¦101765) and told them¦101771, “Go¦101773 \add ≈to Ay\add* and spy¦101774 out the land¦101777.” \add ≈So¦101756\add* the men went¦101778 and checkout out Ay.
\v 3 \add ≈When¦101785\add* they returned¦101785 to Yehoshua¦101788, they told him¦101790, “Don't \add ≈send all¦101794 the¦101796 warriors\add*—\add only\add* around two¦101797 to three¦101800 thousand¦101797 men should¦101793 go¦101803 and¦101785 attack¦101804 them¦101804. Don't \add ≈bother everyone¦101796 else\add* because¦101818 \add ≈Ay¦101807 is¦101819 small\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦101822\add* around three¦101827 thousand¦101828 \add ≈warriors¦101832\add* went¦101822 to \add attack Ay, but they were defeated\add* and¦101830 had to flee¦101830 \add back\add*.
\v 5 The¦101837 men¦101837 from Ay¦101838 chased¦101842 them from the city gate¦101844 downhill to¦101843 Shevarim¦101847 and fought them on¦101849 the slopes. About¦101839 thirty-six¦101839 \add ≈of¦101836 them\add* were¦101854 killed¦101835, and the \add ≈Israelis¦101853 became very afraid and lost all their courage\add*.
\p
\v 6 Yehoshua¦101858 and the¦101865 Israeli¦101872 elders¦101872 tore¦101857 their clothes¦101859 \add in grief\add* and fell¦101860 to¦101865 their knees in front¦101865 of¦101866 Yahweh's¦101867 box¦101866 until¦101868 evening¦101870, throwing dust¦101875 onto their heads¦101878 \add in despair\add*.
\v 7 Then¦101880 Yehoshua¦101881 \add ≈asked\add*, “Yahweh¦101885, my¦101884 master¦101884, why¦101886 did you¦101887 bring \add #these\add* people¦101891 across the Yordan¦101905 and then¦101880 let us¦101897 be defeated and killed by the Amorites¦101899? If¦101901 only we'd been¦101902 content and stayed on¦101898 the other¦101904 side¦101904 of¦101904 the river.
\v 8 Please¦101914, my¦101908 master¦101908, what¦101909 can I¦101910 say¦101910 now that¦101912 \add *we¦101913\add* have had to¦101916 flee \add in shame\add* from our enemies¦101917?
\v 9 \add When\add* the Canaanites¦101920 and the other people living in this land¦101923 hear¦101919 \add <about¦101922 this\add*, they'll¦101919 surround¦101924 us and \add ≈kill all¦101921 of¦101929 us\add*. Then¦101919 what¦101933 would you¦101935 do¦101935 to defend your¦101936 honour?
\p
\v 10 \add ≈But¦101940\add* Yahweh¦101941 told Yehoshua¦101944, “Stand¦101945 up¦101945! Why is¦101949 your¦101953 face¦101953 \add ≈on¦101951 the ground like that¦101948\add*?
\v 11 Yisrael¦101956 has¦101955 sinned¦101955 and disobeyed my¦101961 agreement¦101961\f + \fr 7:11 \ft Probably referring to the ten commands written on the stone slabs.\f* that¦101962 I¦101963 made with them¦101964. They've also¦101957 taken¦101966 prohibited things¦101969—stealing¦101971, deceiving¦101973, and put¦101975 it¦101955 with their¦101976 own possessions.
\v 12 \add That's why\add* \add *they\add* were unable to defeat their¦101984 enemies—they had¦101990 to flee from¦102001 them because¦101989 they took what was prohibited. I¦101993 won't¦101978 be¦101994 with¦101995 you all again unless you all destroy¦101991 \add ≈what was taken\add*.
\v 13 \add So\add* get up and tell the¦102015 people¦102007, ‘Purify yourselves¦102009 for¦102010 tomorrow¦102010, because¦102011 \add *our\add* God¦102015 Yahweh¦102014 says¦102013 that \add ≈we took something prohibited and we won't¦102020 be¦102021 able¦102021 to¦102022 better our enemies¦102024 until¦102025 it's removed¦102027 from¦102029 among us\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈Tomorrow morning¦102032\add* you¦102031 all must present yourselves by your tribes¦102033. Then the tribe¦102035 that Yahweh \add ≈singles out\add*, must present yourselves by your clans¦102041, and¦102031 the clan that Yahweh \add ≈singles out\add*, must present yourselves by household. Then the household that Yahweh \add ≈singles out\add*, must present yourselves individually.
\v 15 The¦102057 \add >man¦102057\add* who¦102057 is¦102057 caught¦102057 will¦102059 be¦102059 destroyed by¦102057 fire¦102060, along with¦102058 everything that¦102066 belongs to¦102068 him¦102068, because¦102075 he's¦102059 violated Yahweh's¦102074 agreement¦102073 and¦102056 committed a disgraceful¦102078 sin among Yisrael¦102079.”
\rem /s1 Achan's Sin
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦102081\add* Yehoshua¦102082 got up early¦102081 the next morning¦102083 and \add ≈ordered each tribe to¦102088 come forward singly\add*, and the tribe of¦102090 Yehudah¦102091 was¦102089 \add ≈singled out\add*.
\v 17 Then¦102093 each of¦102096 the clans came forward and the Zerahite clan was \add ≈singled out\add*, and when their families¦102107 came forwards, Zabdi's¦102109 household was \add ≈singled out\add*.
\v 18 When¦102111 everyone in that \add ≈extended family¦102114\add* came forward¦102111, Achan¦102117 (son of Karmi¦102120, son of Zabdi¦102123, son of Zerah¦102126, from the¦102127 tribe¦102127 of Yehudah¦102128) was¦102116 \add ≈singled out\add*.
\v 19 Then¦102130 Yehoshua¦102131 told Achan¦102134, “My son¦102135, now \add ≈honour\add* Yahweh¦102140 the¦102141 god¦102141 of¦102141 Yisrael¦102142 and¦102130 give¦102143 thanks to¦102145 him¦102145. And¦102147 tell¦102147 me now what¦102151 you've done¦102152—don't¦102153 hide¦102155 it¦102130 from¦102156 me.”
\p
\v 20 “It's true,” Achan¦102159 replied¦102163, “I've¦102166 sinned¦102166 against Yahweh¦102167 the¦102168 god¦102168 of¦102168 Yisrael¦102169. This¦102170 is what I did¦102172:
\v 21 I saw¦102174 a \add ≈beautiful Babylonian cloak¦102177\add* and two¦102181 hundred silver pieces and a tongue-shaped¦102184 piece of¦102189 gold¦102185 (weighing¦102189 six-hundred grams) \add there inside Yeriho/Jericho\add*. I wanted them so I took¦102191 them, and they're¦102192 hidden¦102193 in¦102176 the ground under¦102198 my¦102196 tent¦102196, with¦102176 the silver underneath¦102198.”
\p
\v 22 Yehoshua¦102201 sent¦102200 some messengers¦102202 and they¦102203 ran¦102203 to¦102204 the tent¦102204, and sure enough, it¦102206 was¦102206 all hidden¦102206 there \add in the ground\add* with¦102207 the silver¦102208 underneath¦102209.
\v 23 They¦102211 took¦102211 it out of the tent¦102213 and brought¦102214 it back to¦102215 Yehoshua¦102217 and all¦102219 the people¦102221, and spread¦102223 it out in¦102224 front¦102224 of Yahweh¦102225.
\p
\v 24 Then¦102227 Yehoshua¦102228 took¦102227 Achan¦102231 and the silver¦102237, the cloak¦102240, the gold¦102244 along with his children and his animals, his tent¦102262 and everything he¦102227 owned, and took them¦102275 to¦102269 the Akor¦102277 Valley¦102276 along with all¦102265 the people,
\v 25 and he¦102279 said¦102279, “Why¦102281 did you cause trouble for us¦102282? Yahweh¦102284 will¦102283 trouble you today.” And¦102287 \add ≈the people executed him by throwing rocks at him\add*. Then¦102279 they¦102293 threw rocks at them¦102294 \add all\add* and burnt¦102293 \add the bodies\add*
\v 26 and piled rocks¦102304 over them which are still there¦102313 to this day and Yahweh's¦102310 \add ≈anger¦102312 subsided\add*. That's¦102319 why that¦102308 place¦102318 is called¦102316 ‘Akor¦102321’ \add (i.e., ‘Trouble’)\add* Valley¦102320 to this day.
\c 8
\s1 The defeat and destruction of Ay
