\v 11 and Gilead¦105564, and the territory¦105565 of¦105565 the Geshurites¦105566 and the Maacathites¦105567, and all Mt¦105569. Hermon¦105570, and all the Bashan¦105573 as far as Salekah¦105576,
\v 12 all¦105578 the kingdom¦105580 of Og¦105581 in the Bashan¦105582, who¦105583 reigned¦105585 in Ashtaroth¦105586 and in Edrei¦105587 (what remained from the remnant¦105590 of the Refa'ites¦105591). Mosheh¦105593 \add ≈had¦105592 attacked them¦105592 and captured their lands\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈But¦105596\add* the \add ≈Israelis\add* didn't¦105596 \add ≈capture the land of¦105609\add* the Geshurites¦105607 or the Maacathites¦105608 and¦105596 \add ≈so those peoples¦105598\add* live \add ≈among the Israelis\add* to this¦105613 day¦105612.
\rem /s1 An Inheritance for the Tribe of Levi
\p
\v 14 The¦105616 only¦105615 tribe that didn't¦105618 receive an¦105620 inheritance was¦105626 the tribe of¦105621 Levi¦105617 because the offerings¦105621 given¦105619 to¦105630 Yisrael's¦105624 god¦105623 Yahweh¦105622 are their¦105626 inheritance, just¦105627 like he'd told them.\x + \xo 13:14: \xt Deu 18:1.\x*
