\p
\v 24 This¦105775 was the land that Mosheh¦105769 gave¦105768 to the tribe¦105770 of¦105773 Gad¦105772, according to their¦105776 clans¦105776:
\v 25 It¦105778 included Yazer¦105781 and all¦105782 the cities¦105784 of Gilead¦105785 and half¦105786 of the land¦105787 \add ≈where the Ammonites¦105789 had lived\add* as far as Aroer¦105792 \add ≈opposite\add* Rabbah¦105797,
\v 26 then¦105799 from Heshbon to Ramat¦105802-Mizpah¦105803 and Betonim¦105804, and from Mahanaim¦105805 to the¦105808 Debir border.
\v 27 \add ≈Also¦105811\add* in¦105811 the valley¦105811, Beyt-Haram¦105813, Beyt-Nimrah, Succot¦105816, Zafon¦105817, and the rest of the kingdom¦105819 of Sihon¦105820 (the king¦105821 of Heshbon¦105822), with¦105811 the Yordan and the border¦105824, as far as the end¦105827 of Lake Galilee, eastward¦105833 beyond the Yordan \add River\add*.
\v 28 So that was¦105836 the inheritance¦105836 of¦105836 Gad's¦105839 descendants¦105837—all the cities¦105841 and¦105842 their villages¦105842 allocated to¦105840 their clans¦105840.
