\p
\v 1 These¦105928 are¦105929 what the \add ≈Israelis\add* inherited¦105931 in¦105935 the land¦105935 of Canaan¦105936, which¦105937 Eleazar¦105940 the priest¦105941 and Yehoshua¦105942 (Nun's¦105945 son¦105943) and the \add ≈leaders\add* of the \add ≈Israelis\add* gave¦105938 them¦105939 as¦105938 an inheritance¦105931.
\v 2 Their \add ≈allocations were made by¦105957 casting lots\add* for¦105960 the¦105952 nine¦105960 and¦105962 a half¦105962 tribes¦105961, just¦105954 as¦105954 Yahweh¦105956 had¦105955 commanded¦105955 \add ≈through\add* Mosheh¦105959.\x + \xo 14:2: \xt Num 26:52-56; 34:13.\x*
\v 3 (Mosheh¦105968 had¦105967 given the other two¦105970 and¦105972 a half¦105972 tribes¦105971 their¦105981 inheritance on¦105981 the other side¦105974 of¦105975 the river, but¦105972 the Levites¦105976 weren't given land as an¦105980 inheritance\x + \xo 14:3-4: \xt Num 32:33; 34:14-15; Deu 3:12-17.\x*—
\v 4 instead of¦105986 land¦106006 they¦105985 were given¦105995 cities¦106002 to¦105997 live¦106003 in¦106003, along with the¦105986 \add surrounding\add* fields for¦106005 their¦106005 livestock¦106005. Yosef's¦105988 two sons Menashsheh¦105991 and¦106006 Efrayim¦105992 were considered as two tribes¦105990.)
\v 5 The¦106016 \add ≈Israelis¦106017\add* did¦106015 just¦106008 as Yahweh¦106010 had¦106009 commanded¦106009 Mosheh¦106013—they¦106015 allocated blocks of¦106016 the¦106021 land¦106021 \add as permanent possessions\add*.
\s1 Hebron is allocated to Caleb
\rem /s1 Hebron Allotted to Caleb; Caleb Requests His Land; Hebron Is Given to Caleb; Hebron Given to Caleb
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 6 \add ≈Leaders from the tribe of\add* Yehudah¦106027 approached¦106024 Yehoshua¦106030 at Gilgal¦106031 and Caleb¦106034 (son¦106035 of Yefunneh¦106037 the Kenizzite¦106038) said¦106032 to¦106028 him¦106033, “You¦106039 yourself know¦106040 what Yahweh¦106047 told the man¦106051 of God¦106053 Mosheh¦106050 at Kadesh¦106058-Barnea about¦106056 me and you¦106040.\x + \xo 14:6: \xt Num 14:30.\x*
\v 7 I was¦106061 \add ≈forty¦106063 years¦106064 old\add* when¦106066 Yahweh's¦106070 servant¦106068 Mosheh¦106067 sent¦106066 me¦106071 from¦106072 Kadesh¦106072-Barnea to¦106074 spy¦106074 out¦106074 the¦106077 land¦106077, and¦106078 I brought¦106078 back¦106078 \add ≈an honest report\add*.\x + \xo 14:7: \xt Num 13:1-30.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈The¦106096 other men\add* who¦106087 went¦106088 made the¦106093 \add ≈people¦106094 terrified\add*, \add ≈but¦106086\add* I¦106095 \add ≈remained loyal to\add* my¦106099 god¦106099 Yahweh¦106098.
\v 9 Mosheh¦106102 \add ≈promised me\add* that day¦106103, saying¦106105, ‘The¦106109 land¦106109 \add ≈that you walked on¦106113\add* will¦106115 certainly be for an¦106116 inheritance¦106116 for you and¦106101 your¦106117 sons \add ≈forever¦106120\add*, because¦106121 you were \add ≈completely loyal to¦106105\add* my¦106125 god¦106125 Yahweh¦106124.’\x + \xo 14:9: \xt Num 14:24.\x*
\v 10 Now¦106127, listen. Yahweh has¦106129 kept me¦106132 alive these forty-five¦106136 years¦106138 since Yahweh said that¦106135 to¦106146 Mosheh¦106148, \add back\add* when¦106149 Yisrael¦106152 was¦106158 walking¦106151 in¦106153 the¦106144 wilderness¦106153. \add ≈Yes, believe it¦106151 or not, I'm now¦106154 eighty-five¦106161.\add*
\v 11 I'm still as strong¦106166 today as \add I was\add* on¦106168 the day¦106168 that Mosheh¦106171 sent¦106169 me¦106170. \add ≈Just¦106167 like I could fight back then¦106173, I can still fight or travel just¦106167 the same\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈So\add* now, please give¦106181 me that hill¦106186 country¦106186 that Yahweh \add ≈promised\add* that day¦106198, because¦106194 you¦106195 yourself heard¦106197 \add ≈me say\add* that the¦106186 Anakim¦106202 lived there¦106203 in¦106198 fortified¦106206 cities¦106204. \add So now,\add* perhaps¦106207 Yahweh will¦106209 help me to¦106183 take them¦106210 over just¦106211 as¦106211 \add *he¦106212\add* said.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈So¦106215\add* Yehoshua¦106216 blessed¦106215 Yefunneh's¦106224 son¦106222 \add @Caleb¦106221\add* and¦106217 gave¦106217 him¦106215 Hebron¦106220 as his inheritance¦106225.
\v 14 Because¦106242 of¦106234 that¦106241, Hebron¦106232 belongs¦106230 to Caleb¦106233 (Yefunneh¦106236 the¦106234 Kenizzite's¦106237 son¦106234) as an¦106238 inheritance¦106238 until¦106239 this¦106241 day¦106240, because¦106242 he¦106244 was \add ≈completely loyal to\add* Yisrael's¦106248 god¦106247 Yahweh¦106246.
\v 15 (Hebron¦106251 used to be called Kiriat¦106254-Arba—\add @Arba\add* had been a \add ≈brave warrior\add* among¦106257 the¦106255 Anakim¦106257.)
\p Then¦106250 there was¦106260 a time of¦106250 no more war¦106261 in¦106257 that region.
\c 15
\s1 The area assigned to Yehudah's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory of Judah; The Land Given to the Tribe of Judah; Allotment for Judah; The Territory Assigned to Judah
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add This was the land\add* that was assigned to Yehudah's¦106268 descendants¦106267 according to their¦106269 clans¦106269:
\p It¦106264 went from¦106278 the Zin¦106276 wilderness¦106274 in the south¦106277 to¦106269 the border¦106272 with Edom¦106273,
\v 2 and¦106281 their southern¦106284 border¦106283 was¦106281 the south-facing¦106284 bay at the end¦106285 of¦106286 the \add ≈Dead Sea\add* \add (also called the Salt Sea)\add*.
\v 3 \add From there\add* it¦106300 went south¦106297 of¦106299 the¦106297 Scorpion¦106299 Pass, across to Zin¦106301, \add ≈climbed\add* up¦106302 to Kadesh¦106304-Barnea, crossed to Hezron¦106307, went to Addar¦106309, and¦106294 around to Karka¦106311.
\v 4 Then¦106313 it¦106325 crosses to Azmon¦106314 and out¦106315 to the Egyptian¦106317 riverbed¦106316 and \add ≈finishes\add* at¦106322 the \add Mediterranean\add* sea¦106322. That will¦106325 be¦106325 their southern¦106328 border¦106327.
\p
\v 5 The¦106338 eastern border¦106330 was the \add ≈Dead Sea¦106342\add* as far as the end¦106336 of¦106336 the Yordan¦106337.
\p The northern¦106340 border \add starts\add* at the top of the \add ≈Dead Sea\add* where the Yordan \add river\add* enters it
\v 6 then¦106346 to Beyt-Hoglah¦106349 and¦106346 \add further\add* north¦106351 to Beyt-Aravah to the¦106347 Stone¦106356 of¦106351 Bohan¦106357 (Reuben's¦106360 son¦106360).
\v 7 Then¦106362 the border went¦106362 to Debir¦106365 from the Akor¦106367 Valley¦106366, and to the north¦106368, turning¦106369 to the Gilgal¦106372, which is in front of the Adummim¦106377 pass which is from the south¦106379 of the riverbed¦106380, then¦106362 the border passed¦106381 over to the waters¦106385 of Eyn-Shemesh and its¦106390 ends¦106390 at Eyn-Rogel¦106394.
\v 8 \add ≈From¦106406 there\add* the border went up¦106396 the valley of Ben¦106398 Hinnom to the edge of the Yebusite¦106405 region from¦106406 the south¦106406 (that¦106415 is Yerushalem¦106408). Then¦106396 the border went to the head of the hill¦106414 opposite the Hinnom valley to the west, which¦106423 is at¦106424 the end¦106424 of the valley of the Refa'ites to the north¦106428.
\v 9 \add ≈From¦106432 there\add* the border turned from¦106432 the head of the hill¦106433 to the Neftoah spring¦106436 and¦106430 went¦106439 out¦106439 to the cities¦106442 of Mt¦106433. Efron¦106445, then¦106430 the border turned to Ba'alah (\add ≈now called\add* Kiriat¦106451-Yearim).
\v 10 Then¦106453 the border¦106454 went around from Ba'alah to the west to Mt. Seir¦106460, and passed over to the shoulder of¦106464 Mt. Yearim¦106467 from the north¦106468 (\add ≈also¦106461 called\add* Kesalon¦106470), and went down¦106471 to Beyt¦106472-Shemesh¦106474, and passed over to Timnah¦106476.
\v 11 \add ≈From there\add* the border went out to the shoulder of¦106482 Ekron¦106483 to the north¦106484, then turned¦106485 toward Shikkeron¦106487 and passed¦106488 over to Mt¦106489. Baalah¦106491, and went out to Yabneel, then the border ended at¦106497 the sea¦106497.
\v 12 The¦106499 western border¦106499 was the \add ≈Mediterranean\add* Sea¦106501. Those were the borders¦106505 of¦106505 \add the land given to\add* Yehudah's¦106508 descendants¦106506 to be allocated to their¦106510 clans¦106510.
\s1 Caleb defeats Hebron and Debir
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Caleb; Caleb Occupies His Portion; Caleb Conquers Hebron and Debir
\s4 Promised land
\r (Jdg. 1:11-15)
\p
\v 13 Yahweh¦106525 had instructed Yehoshua¦106526 to give¦106516 \add this\add* block of¦106513 land to Caleb (Yefunneh's¦106515 son¦106513): Kiriat¦106529-Arba (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦106534—Arba was¦106534 Anak's¦106532 father¦106531).\x + \xo 15:13-14: \xt Jdg 1:20.\x*
\v 14 Caleb¦106538 captured \add the land\add* from¦106537 Anak's¦106543 three¦106541 sons¦106542—Sheshai¦106546, Ahiman¦106549, and¦106536 Talmai¦106552,
\v 15 then¦106556 from¦106557 there¦106557, he¦106556 \add ≈battled against¦106558\add* Debir¦106561 (formerly¦106565 called Kiriat¦106568-Sefer¦106564)
\v 16 and \add *he¦106570\add* said¦106570, “I'll¦106581 give¦106581 my¦106586 daughter¦106586 Aksah¦106585 to marry \add ≈to the¦106572 man who¦106572 attacks¦106574\add* Kiriat¦106577-Sefer and captures¦106580 it¦106570.”
\v 17 Then¦106589 Othniel¦106590 (Kenaz's¦106593 son¦106591 and¦106596 Caleb's¦106595 brother¦106594) captured¦106589 \add @the¦106591 city\add*, \add ≈so\add* Caleb gave¦106596 his¦106602 daughter¦106602 Aksah¦106601 to¦106603 him¦106598 for¦106603 a wife.
\v 18 Then¦106605 \add ≈when¦106606 she married him\add*, she \add ≈encouraged\add* him to ask¦106608 her father¦106611 for¦106618 a field¦106612, \add ≈so\add* she got down¦106613 off her donkey¦106615 and¦106605 Caleb¦106619 asked, “What¦106620 \add ≈are you¦106622 up to\add*?”
\v 19 “Give¦106625 me a blessing¦106628,” she¦106624 answered¦106624, “because¦106629 you've¦106632 given¦106632 me land¦106630 in the Negev¦106631 \add desert region\add*, \add ≈so now\add* give¦106633 me some springs \add as well\add* for¦106639 water¦106636.” \add ≈So¦106624\add* he¦106637 gave¦106637 her¦106639 \add both\add* the upper¦106642 and¦106624 the lower¦106645 springs.
