\p
\v 55 \add Also\add* Maon¦106882, Karmel¦106884, Zif¦106885, Yuttah,
\v 56 Yezreel, Yokdeam¦106889, Zanoah¦106890,
\v 57 Kayin, Gibeah¦106893, and¦106894 Timnah¦106894—ten¦106896 cities¦106895 as well as their¦106897 villages¦106897.
\p
\v 58 \add Also\add* Halhul¦106899, Beyt¦106900-Zur¦106902, Gedor¦106903,
\v 59 Maarat¦106905, Beyt¦106906-Anot, and¦106905 Eltekon¦106909—six¦106911 cities¦106910 as well as their¦106912 villages¦106912.
\p
\v 60 \add Also\add* Kiriat-Baal¦106916 (\add ≈also¦106920 called\add* Kiriat-Yearim¦106919) and¦106923 Rabbah¦106920—two¦106922 cities¦106921 as well as their¦106923 villages¦106923.
\p
\v 61 In¦106926 the wilderness¦106926, Beyt¦106927-Aravah¦106928, Middin¦106929, Secacah¦106930,
\v 62 Nibshan¦106932, the¦106932 City¦106933 of¦106933 Salt¦106935, and¦106932 Eyn¦106936-Gedi—six¦106939 cities¦106938 as well as their¦106940 villages¦106940.
\p
\v 63 \add ≈But¦106942\add* Yehudah's¦106953 descendants¦106951 weren't able¦106949 to defeat the Yebusites¦106944 who lived in¦106961 Yerushalem¦106946, so \add *they¦106949\add* have lived among the tribe of¦106959 Yehudah to this¦106964 day¦106963.\x + \xo 15:63: \xt Jdg 1:21; 2Sam 5:6; 1Ch 11:4.\x*
\c 16
\s1 The allocation to Yosef's descendants
\rem /s1 Allotment for Ephraim and Manasseh; The Inheritance of Ephraim and West Manasseh; The Territory Assigned to Ephraim and West Manasseh; The Territory of Ephraim
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The¦106968 block for Yosef's¦106970 descendants¦106969\f + \fr 16:1 \ft i.e., the half-tribes of Efrayim and Menashsheh.\f* went¦106967 from¦106971 the Yordan¦106971 at¦106979 Yeriho¦106974 (\add Jericho\add*, east of the \add ≈springs\add*), through the wilderness¦106976 into the hill country¦106979 of Beyt¦106980-El.
\v 2 It¦106984 went¦106984 out¦106984 from¦106985 Beyt¦106985-El to¦106988 Luz¦106988 then¦106984 along¦106989 the border¦106992 with the Arkites¦106993 at Atarot¦106994.
\v 3 Then¦106996 it¦107013 went¦106996 west to the border with the Yafletites as far as the border with Lower¦107008 Beyt¦107005-Horon¦107007 and¦106996 as far as Gezer¦107011, then¦106996 out to the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*.
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Ephraim
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦107017\add* Yosef's¦107020 sons Menashsheh¦107021 and¦107022 Efrayim¦107022 received¦107017 an inheritance¦107017.
\s1 The allocation to Efrayim's descendants
\rem /s1 Ephraim
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 5 The¦107025 allotment for Efrayim's¦107028 descendants¦107026 according to¦107029 their¦107029 clans¦107029 was¦107030 at Atarot¦107034-Addar¦107035 in the¦107031 east, going as far as Upper¦107040 Beyt¦107038-Horon¦107039
\v 6 and¦107042 out¦107042 to the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*. From¦107046 Mikmetat in the north¦107046, the border¦107048 went¦107042 eastward¦107049 toward Taanat¦107050-Shiloh¦107051 then¦107042 further east¦107054 to Yanoah¦107055.
\v 7 From¦107058 Yanoah¦107058 it¦107061 went¦107057 to¦107060 Atarot¦107059 and¦107057 Naarah¦107060, reached Yeriho¦107062 \add !(Jericho¦107062)\add* then¦107057 came¦107063 out¦107063 at¦107062 the¦107064 Yordan¦107064.
\v 8 \add The northern border went\add* from¦107066 Tappuah to the Kanah¦107071 riverbed¦107070 and¦107072 then out to the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*. That was¦107076 the inheritance¦107076 of¦107076 Efrayim's¦107080 descendants¦107078 according to their¦107081 clans¦107081,
\v 9 \add ≈although\add* some of¦107085 the cities¦107083 with their¦107095 villages¦107095 for¦107085 Efrayim's¦107086 descendants were \add actually\add* inside the territory assigned to Menashsheh's¦107091 descendants.
\v 10 \add ≈But¦107097\add* they didn't¦107097 \add ≈capture the land of¦107106\add* the Canaanites¦107101 who¦107102 lived in¦107103 Gezer¦107103, so they've lived within Efrayim¦107107 to this¦107111 day¦107110 and¦107097 were forced¦107113 to serve as labourers¦107113.\x + \xo 16:10: \xt Jdg 1:29.\x*
\c 17
\s1 The allocation to Menashsheh's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to West Manasseh; West Manasseh; The Other Half-Tribe of Manasseh (West)
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The¦107119 allotment for Menashsheh's¦107121 descendants (Yosef's¦107126 eldest son) \add included a special allotment for\add* (Gilead's¦107131 father¦107130) Makir¦107127—he was given Gilead and¦107137 Bashan¦107141 because¦107122 he was a \add ≈powerful warrior\add*.
\v 2 The¦107144 other Menashsheh clans \add that were allocated land\add* were the Abiezer¦107149, Helek¦107152, Asriel¦107154, Shekem¦107157, Hefer¦107160, and¦107143 Shemida¦107162 clans. (They were the sons¦107166 of¦107164 Yosef's¦107168 son¦107166 Menashsheh \add who led their own\add* clans.)
\v 3 \add ≈But¦107172\add* Zelofehad (son of Hefer¦107175, son of Gilead¦107178, son of Makir¦107181, son of Menashsheh¦107184) had no sons¦107189—only daughters¦107193 who were¦107195 named Mahlah¦107197, Noah¦107198, Hoglah¦107199, Milkah¦107200, and¦107172 Tirzah¦107201.
\v 4 They¦107203 approached the priest¦107206 Eleazar¦107205 and Yehoshua¦107209 and the other leaders¦107214 and said¦107215, “Yahweh told¦107217 Mosheh¦107220 to¦107215 give¦107221 us¦107223 an inheritance along with our¦107226 brothers¦107226.” \add ≈So¦107203\add* he\f + \fr 17:4 \ft It's not clear who this ‘he’ refers to here—some translations choose Eleazar (implied by the sentence structure) and others choose Yehoshua (implied by past allocations of land).\f* gave¦107227 them an inheritance (like he'd given their¦107236 uncles), as Yahweh \add ≈had instructed¦107217 them\add*.\x + \xo 17:4: \xt Num 27:1-7.\x*
\v 5 \add ≈So¦107238\add* ten¦107242 blocks were allocated to Menashsheh¦107241 \add tribe\add* as well as Gilead¦107245 and¦107238 Bashan¦107246 which¦107247 were across the¦107239 Yordan¦107249
\v 6 because¦107251 Menashsheh's daughters¦107252 received inheritances¦107254 along with his¦107257 sons. The¦107258 land¦107258 of Gilead¦107259 belonged¦107260 to¦107261 the¦107261 rest of Menashsheh's sons.
\p
\v 7 The¦107267 border¦107267 for Menashsheh¦107269 went from¦107270 Asher¦107270 to¦107279 Mikmetat \add ≈opposite\add* Shekem¦107276, then¦107266 went \add ≈south¦107281\add* towards the¦107281 spring at Tappuah.
\v 8 (The¦107290 Tappuah \em land¦107290\em* was for Menashsheh¦107296, but¦107292 Tappuah \add town\add* was for Efrayim¦107298.)
\v 9 Then¦107300 the border went¦107300 south¦107304 to the Kanah¦107303 riverbed—the cities¦107306 there belonged¦107308 to Efrayim¦107308 even though they were inside Menashsheh's¦107311 land—then¦107300 the border stayed on the north¦107314 side of¦107314 the riverbed and¦107300 extended to the \add ≈Mediterranean¦107313\add*.
\v 10 \add So\add* the south was for Efrayim¦107321 and the north was for Menashsheh¦107323, and the sea¦107325 was the \add western\add* border¦107326, meeting Asher¦107327 from the north and Yissakar¦107330 from the east¦107331.
\v 11 Menashsheh¦107334 was¦107333 allocated cities inside \add both\add* Yissakar's¦107335 and Asher's¦107336 territories: Beyt¦107337-Shan¦107339, Ibleam¦107341, Dor¦107346, Endor¦107351, Taanach¦107354, and Megiddo¦107357 along with¦107335 their \add ≈surrounding towns\add*.\f + \fr 17:11 \ft We've omitted the final Hebrew phrase here (the three of Nafet) since it's unclear what it means (plus it's not considered to be a vital point in the narrative).\f*
\v 12 \add ≈But¦107362\add* Menashsheh's¦107365 descendants¦107364 weren't able¦107363 to take¦107366 possession¦107366 of¦107366 those¦107370 cities¦107369, \add ≈so\add* the Canaanites¦107372 continued to live¦107373 in the region.\x + \xo 17:12-13: \xt Jdg 1:27-28.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈When¦107377 the¦107380 Israelis¦107381 strengthened their position\add*, they were¦107377 able to force¦107386 those Canaanites¦107385 to work¦107386 for them, \add ≈but¦107377\add* they weren't able to \add ≈drive them out\add*.
\s1 Efrayim and Menashsheh's descendants are given additional land
\rem /s1 The Tribe of Joseph Protests; Ephraim and West Manasseh Request More Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 14 Then the¦107393 \add two\add* \add ≈half-tribes of¦107393 Efrayim and¦107405 Menashsheh\add* asked Yehoshua¦107397, “Why¦107399 have¦107400 you¦107400 \add only\add* given¦107400 to¦107401 \add #us\add* one¦107406 measured allocation as an¦107402 inheritance¦107402 when \add #we're\add* \add very\add* numerous¦107410 \add because\add* Yahweh¦107418 has¦107417 \add ≈already\add* blessed¦107417 \add #us\add*?”
\p
\v 15 “If¦107423 \add ≈there's¦107434 so¦107434 many¦107434 of you\add*,” Yehoshua¦107422 \add ≈answered¦107420\add*, “and if¦107423 Efrayim's¦107444 hill-country is¦107440 too small for you, go¦107429 into the forested¦107431 area of the Perizzites¦107436 and the Refaites¦107437 and clear¦107432 some land¦107435 for yourselves¦107441 there.”
\p
\v 16 “The¦107447 hill¦107453 country¦107453 \add certainly\add* isn't¦107449 big enough for¦107452 \add all of\add* us¦107452,” \add *they¦107446\add* responded¦107446, “plus¦107454 the Canaanites¦107458 living in the Yezreel¦107470 valley¦107462 and in Beyt-Shan and the surrounding towns have iron¦107455 chariots¦107454.”
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦107472\add* Yehoshua¦107473 told the¦107476 \add ≈half-tribes of Efrayim¦107478 and Menashsheh¦107479\add*, “\add Yes\add*, there's a¦107481 lot¦107492 of you and you're very powerful¦107485. One¦107493 land allotment \add ≈wouldn't be¦107481 enough for¦107487 you\add*
\v 18 \add ≈so\add* the hill¦107496 country¦107496 will¦107497 be yours¦107506 \add as well\add*. \add ≈However\add*, it's¦107503 a forest¦107502 and you'll¦107504 have to clear¦107504 it to the borders¦107507. You'll \add need to\add* drive out the Canaanites¦107513 even if¦107518 they are strong¦107519 and with iron¦107516 chariots¦107515.”
\c 18
\s1 Allocations for the remaining seven tribes
\rem /s1 The Territories of the Remaining Tribes; Division of the Rest of the Land; The Allotments of the Remaining Land; The Division of the Rest of the Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then all¦107524 the Israelis¦107529 assembled¦107523 at Shiloh¦107530 and¦107531 set up the sacred¦107535 tent¦107535 there¦107532. The¦107537 \add ≈battles over the land had stopped\add*
\v 2 but¦107541 seven¦107551 of¦107542 \add *their\add* tribes¦107552 hadn't had¦107547 their inheritances¦107550 assigned \add yet\add*.
\v 3 Yehoshua¦107555 asked the Israelis¦107559, “\add ≈How much longer are¦107564 you all going¦107565 to¦107565 put off capturing\add* the land¦107569 that¦107570 your ancestors' God¦107574 Yahweh¦107573 has¦107571 given¦107571 you?
\v 4 Choose three¦107579 men¦107580 from each \add of those seven\add*\f + \fr 18:4 \ft Not in the Hebrew but implied by verse 5 as they go on to divide the surveyed land into seven portions.\f* tribes¦107581 and I'll send¦107582 them¦107582 out to \add ≈scout around\add* \add and inspect\add* the¦107585 land and write¦107586 \add ≈descriptions¦107586 of it in¦107585 terms of potential allocations and bring it\add* to me¦107591.
\v 5 They¦107593 can divide¦107593 \add @that¦107593 land¦107593\add* into¦107595 seven¦107595 parts. (Yehudah¦107597 will¦107598 maintain their¦107608 territory¦107601 in the south¦107602, and¦107603 Yosef's¦107604 tribes in the north¦107609.)
\v 6 You all should write¦107612 descriptions¦107612 of the seven parts and bring¦107618 them here¦107624 to me¦107619, and in¦107612 front¦107625 of our¦107627 god¦107627 Yahweh¦107626, I'll¦107621 throw¦107621 dice for¦107622 you \add to allocate them to the seven tribes\add*.
\v 7 However, the Levites¦107633 don't¦107630 receive a portion¦107632, because¦107635 their inheritance is¦107637 Yahweh's priesthood¦107637. Gad¦107640 and Reuven¦107641 and the Menashsheh¦107644 half-tribe have¦107645 \add already\add* received¦107645 their inheritance that¦107650 Yahweh's servant¦107654 Mosheh¦107653 allocated to¦107649 them¦107652 on¦107634 the eastern¦107649 side¦107647 of¦107654 the Yordan¦107648.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦107657\add* the¦107658 \add chosen\add* men¦107658 \add ≈got ready to leave\add* and Yehoshua¦107661 instructed¦107660 them, “Go¦107670 and walk¦107671 around that¦107664 land¦107668 and write¦107673 \add a report\add* and \add ≈bring it¦107674 back\add* to me¦107676. Then¦107657 I'll¦107678 throw¦107678 dice for¦107679 you all \add ≈in front¦107681\add* of¦107681 Yahweh¦107682 here¦107677 in Shiloh¦107683.”
\v 9 Then¦107685 the men¦107686 left and¦107685 \add ≈walked through the area\add*, writing¦107689 down \add their recommendations\add* for dividing the seven¦107691 portions¦107692 according to the cities¦107690 \add in the area\add*, then¦107685 they¦107696 returned back to Yehoshua¦107699 at the camp¦107702 at Shiloh¦107703.
\v 10 \add ≈So¦107705\add* Yehoshua¦107707 threw¦107705 dice for¦107706 them¦107706 at Shiloh¦107709 \add ≈in¦107709 front¦107710\add* of¦107710 Yahweh¦107711, and¦107705 \add ≈so that land¦107718 was allocated to¦107719 those¦107706 remaining seven tribes\add*.
\s1 The allocation to Benyamin's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Benjamin; The Territory of Benjamin; Allotment for Benjamin; The Territory Assigned to Benjamin
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 11 The¦107725 tribe¦107726 of¦107725 Benyamin¦107729 won the \add first\add* draw and the area for their¦107730 clans¦107730 was between¦107734 the land assigned to Yehudah¦107736 and that assigned to \add ≈Efrayim and Menashsheh\add*.
\v 12 Their northern border¦107743 went from¦107746 the Yordan¦107748 then¦107741 to the northern side¦107744 of¦107753 Yeriho¦107754 \add !(Jericho¦107754)\add* and¦107741 up¦107749 into the hill country¦107757 to the west, coming¦107759 out in¦107757 the wilderness¦107762 at¦107757 Beyt¦107763-Aven¦107764.
\v 13 Then¦107766 it¦107766 went¦107779 across towards Luz¦107769 (\add ≈now called\add* Beyt-El) to¦107769 the southern¦107774 edge then¦107766 downhill towards Atarot¦107781-Addar¦107782 beside the hill¦107785 south¦107787 of¦107788 lower¦107791 Beyt-Horon.
\v 14 Then¦107793 the western border¦107794 turned from¦107800 that¦107803 hill¦107802 and¦107793 went¦107811 south¦107810, coming out at Kiriat-Baal¦107818 (\add ≈also¦107795 called\add* Kiriat-Yearim¦107821—a town¦107822 belonging to¦107796 Yehudah¦107824) thus forming the western side¦107826.
\v 15 The¦107830 southern¦107832 border¦107837 went¦107839 west from¦107833 Kiriat¦107835-Yearim to¦107832 the¦107832 spring¦107842 at Neftoah,
\v 16 then downhill to the Ben¦107856-Hinnon valley (in¦107861 the valley of the Refaites¦107862 to the north¦107863) then downhill to Hinnon valley to the edge of the Yebusites¦107870 and¦107846 downhill to Eyn¦107873-Rogel¦107874.
\v 17 Then¦107876 it¦107876 turned¦107876 northward¦107877 and went¦107878 \add west\add* to Eyn¦107879-Shemesh¦107880 and across to Gelilot¦107884 opposite¦107887 the Adummim¦107889 pass, before going downhill to the Stone¦107891 of¦107891 Bohan¦107892 (Reuben's¦107895 son¦107895).
\v 18 It¦107897 extended over to¦107898 the northern¦107904 slope¦107900 of¦107900 the Yordan valley and¦107905 then¦107897 downhill into the \add actual\add* valley.
\v 19 \add *It¦107908\add* then¦107908 went¦107917 \add east\add* to¦107910 the northern¦107916 slope¦107912 of Beyt¦107913-Hoglah¦107915 before coming out at¦107929 the \add ≈north¦107916 end¦107932\add* of the \add ≈Dead Sea\add* \add (also called the Salt Sea)\add* where the Yordan¦107933 river flows into it¦107908. That was the southern¦107934 boundary¦107922
\v 20 and¦107939 the Yordan¦107939 borders it¦107942 on the east. Those were¦107947 the borders of¦107950 Benyamin's¦107949 descendants' inheritance¦107947 according¦107950 to¦107952 their¦107952 clans¦107952.
\rem /s1 The Towns Given to Benjamin
\p
\v 21 The¦107955 cities¦107955 allocated to¦107956 Benyamin's¦107958 descendants¦107957 and¦107954 their¦107959 clans¦107959 were¦107954: Yeriho¦107960 \add !(Jericho¦107960)\add*, Beyt¦107961-Hoglah, Emek¦107964-Keziz,
\v 22 Beyt-Aravah, Zemaraim¦107969, Beyt-El,
\v 23 Avvim¦107974, Parah¦107975, Ofrah¦107976,
\v 24 Kefar-Ammoni¦107978, Ofni, and¦107978 Geba¦107982—a total of¦107987 twelve cities¦107983 as well as their¦107987 \add surrounding\add* villages¦107987.
\v 25 \add Also\add* Gibeon, Ramah¦107990, Beerot¦107991,
\v 26 Mizpah, Kefirah¦107994, Mozah¦107995,
\v 27 Rekem¦107997, Irpeel¦107998, Taralah¦107999,
\v 28 Zelah, Haelef¦108002, Yebus¦108003 (\add ≈now called\add* Yerushalem¦108006), Gibeah¦108007, and¦108001 Kiriat¦108008—\add a total of\add* fourteen cities¦108009 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108013. Those were Benyamin's¦108018 descendants' inheritance¦108015 according to¦108019 their clans¦108019.
\c 19
\s1 The allocation to Shimeon's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory Assigned to Simeon; The Land Given to Simeon; The Territory of Simeon; Allotment for Simeon
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The¦108023 second¦108024 draw went¦108022 to¦108030 Shimeon's¦108029 (Simeon's¦108025) descendants¦108027 and¦108031 the land for¦108025 their¦108030 clans¦108030 was¦108031 in¦108033 the middle¦108033 of¦108037 Yehudah's¦108037 territory.
\v 2 Shimeon's¦108045 inheritance¦108041 \add ≈included\add*: Beer¦108042-Sheba¦108044,\f + \fr 19:2 \ft TC: Ancient manuscripts differ, with some adding Sheba (possibly a mistaken reduplication) or Shema here (but that would make the total number wrong that's given in v6).\f* Moladah¦108046,\x + \xo 19:2-8: \xt 1Ch 4:28-33.\x*
\v 3 Hazarshual¦108048, Balah¦108050, Ezem¦108051,
\v 4 Eltolad, Betul¦108054, Hormah¦108055,
\v 5 Ziklag¦108057, Beyt¦108058-Markabot. Hatsarsusah,
\v 6 Beyt-Lebaot, and¦108064 Sharuhen¦108066—thirteen cities¦108067 as well as their¦108071 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108071.
\p
\v 7 \add Also\add* Ain, Rimmon¦108075, Eter¦108076, and¦108077 Asha—four¦108079 cities¦108078 as well as their¦108080 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108080,
\v 8 and¦108082 all¦108082 the \add further\add* villages¦108084 around¦108086 those¦108088 cities¦108087 as far as Baalat¦108091-Beer¦108092 (\add also called\add* Ramah¦108093 of¦108086 the Negev¦108094). That¦108085 was¦108096 Shimeon's¦108100 descendants' inheritance¦108096 according to¦108101 their¦108101 clans¦108101.
\v 9 This \add took away\add* some of¦108103 Yehudah's inheritance¦108106 and¦108118 gave it¦108111 to Shimeons descendants¦108104 because¦108109 Yehudah's \add initial\add* area was¦108111 more than \add ≈they¦108118 needed\add*.
\s1 The allocation to Zebulun's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Zebulun; The Territory of Zebulun; Allotment for Zebulun; The Territory Assigned to Zebulun
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 The third¦108128 draw went to Zebulun's¦108130 descendants¦108129 according to their clans¦108131. The \add southern\add* border¦108133 for¦108129 their inheritance¦108134 \add ≈started\add* at Sarid¦108137
\v 11 and went¦108139 \add west\add* to Maralah¦108143 and Dabbeshet¦108145 then¦108139 to the¦108149 riverbed¦108149 facing Yokneam¦108154.
\v 12 \add Also\add* from¦108157 Sarid¦108157 it¦108156 went toward the east beside the border¦108163 with Kislot¦108165-Tabor and then on to Daberat¦108169 and then to Yafia¦108171.
\v 13 From¦108173 there¦108173 it¦108174 extended east to Gittah-Hefer¦108178 and Ittah-Katsin and \add north\add* to Rimmon¦108182 before turning¦108183 to Neah¦108184.
\v 14 Then¦108186 \add *it¦108186\add* passed north¦108189 of¦108189 Hannaton¦108190 ending at Yiftah¦108194-El¦108196 valley¦108193.
\v 15 \add It included the cities of\add* Kattat¦108198, Nahalal¦108199, Shimron¦108200, Idalah¦108201, and¦108198 Bethlehem—\add a total of\add* twelve cities as well as their¦108208 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108208.
\v 16 That was¦108211 Zebulun's¦108214 descendants' inheritance¦108211 according¦108215 to¦108215 their clans¦108215, \add including\add* those¦108217 cities¦108216 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108218.
\s1 The allocation to Yissakar's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory Assigned to Issachar; Allotment for Issachar; The Territory of Issachar; The Land Given to Issachar
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 17 The¦108226 fourth¦108224 draw went¦108222 to Yissakar's¦108221 descendants¦108225 according¦108227 to their¦108227 clans¦108227.
\v 18 \add ≈Their¦108230 land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Yezreel¦108231, Kesulot¦108232, Shunem¦108233,
\v 19 Hafaraim, Shion¦108236, Anaharat¦108237,
\v 20 Rabbit¦108239, Kishion¦108240, Ebets¦108241,
\v 21 Remet¦108243, Eyn-Gannim, Eyn-Haddah, and¦108243 Beyt¦108249-Pazzets.
\v 22 The¦108253 border¦108253 \add of their allotment\add* met with¦108254 Tabor¦108254, Shahazumah¦108255, and¦108252 Beyt¦108257-Shemesh, coming out \add in the east\add* at¦108254 the Yordan¦108262—\add a total of\add* sixteen cities¦108263 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108267.
\v 23 That was¦108270 Yissakar's¦108274 descendants' inheritance¦108270 according to¦108275 their clans¦108275, \add including\add* those cities¦108276 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108277.
\s1 The allocation to Asher's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory of Asher; Allotment for Asher; The Land Given to Asher; The Territory Assigned to Asher
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 24 The¦108281 fifth¦108282 draw went¦108280 to Asher's¦108286 descendants¦108284 according¦108287 to their¦108287 clans¦108287.
\v 25 \add ≈Their¦108290 land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Helkat¦108291, Hali¦108292, Beten¦108293, Akshaf¦108294,
\v 26 Allammelek¦108296, Amad¦108297, and Mishal¦108298. Their \add western\add* \add @border\add* started at¦108300 Mt. Karmel¦108300 and Shihorlibnat¦108302
\v 27 and turned¦108305 back¦108305 to the east to Beyt-Dagon¦108309 and the border with¦108311 Zebulun¦108311 and the Yiftah-El valley¦108315 to the north. Then¦108305 it¦108305 went¦108320 to Beyt-Emek¦108318 and Neiel¦108319 and north to Kabul,
\v 28 Abdon, Rehob¦108327, Hammon¦108328 and¦108326 Kanah¦108329, as far as Greater¦108332 Sidon¦108331.
\v 29 The¦108335 border¦108344 then¦108334 turned back¦108334 to Ramah¦108336 and to the fortified¦108340 city¦108339 of¦108340 Tsor¦108342 \add (commonly known as Tyre)\add* and turns¦108343 \add ≈west\add* to Hosah¦108345 coming out at the \add @Mediterranean¦108346\add* near Akzib¦108351.
\v 30 \add It also included\add* Ummah¦108353, Afek¦108354, and¦108353 Rehob¦108355—\add a total of\add* twenty-two¦108357 cities¦108356 as well as their¦108359 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108359.
\v 31 That was¦108362 Asher's¦108366 descendants' inheritance¦108362 according to¦108367 their clans¦108367, \add including\add* those¦108369 cities¦108368 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108370.
\s1 The allocation to Naftali's descendants
\rem /s1 Allotment for Naphtali; The Territory Assigned to Naphtali; The Territory of Naphtali; The Land Given to Naphtali
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 32 The¦108379 sixth¦108377 draw went¦108375 to Naftali's¦108374 descendants¦108373 according to their¦108380 clans¦108380.
\v 33 Their¦108383 border¦108383 started in¦108386 Helef (where there was¦108382 an oak tree¦108385 at Zaanannim¦108386) then¦108382 Adami¦108387-Nekeb and Yabneel and on¦108386 to¦108390 Lakkum¦108392 before exiting at the¦108395 Yordan¦108395.
\v 34 Then¦108397 \add *it¦108397\add* turned¦108397 west to Aznot¦108400-Tabor¦108401 and from¦108403 there¦108403 to Hukkok¦108404, meeting \add the border\add* with Zebulun¦108406 on the south¦108407, \add the border\add* with Asher¦108408 on the west, and \add the border\add* with Yehudah¦108411 on the east.
\v 35 The¦108416 fortified¦108417 cities¦108416 were¦108418 Tsiddim, Tser, Hammat¦108420, Rakkat¦108421, Kinneret¦108422,
\v 36 Adamah, Ramah¦108425, Hatsor¦108426,
\v 37 Kedesh, Edrei¦108429, Eyn¦108430-Hatsor,
\v 38 Yiron¦108433, Migdal¦108434-El, Horem¦108437, Beyt-Anat, and¦108433 Beyt-Shemesh—\add a total of\add* nineteen cities¦108443 as well as their¦108447 \add surrounding\add* villages¦108447.
\v 39 That was¦108450 Naftali's¦108454 descendants' inheritance¦108450 according to¦108455 their clans¦108455, \add including\add* those cities¦108456 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108457.
\s1 The allocation to Dan's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Dan; Allotment for Dan; The Territory of Dan; The Territory Assigned to Dan
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 40 The¦108460 \add final\add* seventh¦108467 draw went¦108465 to Dan's¦108463 descendants¦108461 according to their¦108464 clans¦108464.
\v 41 \add ≈Their¦108471 land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Tsorah¦108472, Eshtaol¦108473, Ir-Shemesh¦108474,
\v 42 Shaalabbin¦108477, Ayyalon¦108478, and¦108477 Yitlah¦108479,
\v 43 Elon, Timnah¦108482, Ekron¦108483,
\v 44 Eltekeh¦108485, Gibbeton¦108486, Baalat¦108487,
\v 45 Yehud, Bene-Berak, Gat¦108493-Rimmon,
\v 46 Meyarkon, Rakkon¦108499, and¦108499 the¦108499 area opposite¦108503 Yafo¦108504 \add !(Joppa¦108504)\add*.
\v 47 Dan's border¦108526 went¦108506 out¦108506 from¦108512 them.\f + \fr 19:47 \ft Translations vary widely here because we're not sure what is meant by the literal rendering that we've kept here.\f* Then¦108506 Dan's descendants¦108514 battled against Leshem and captured¦108521 it and \add ≈slaughtered their inhabitants\add*. \add ≈So¦108506\add* they took¦108529 it over and settled in¦108532 Leshem \add ≈but¦108506\add* they renamed it to¦108526 ‘Dan’ after their ancestor¦108538.\x + \xo 19:47: \xt Jdg 18:27-29.\x*
\v 48 That was¦108541 Dan's¦108545 descendants' inheritance¦108541 according to¦108546 their clans¦108546, \add including\add* those¦108548 cities¦108547 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108549.
\s1 Yehoshua's allocation
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Joshua; The Final Assignment of the Land; Allotment for Joshua; Joshua's Inheritance
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 49 \add ≈After the allocation of the blocks of land¦108557 to¦108564 the various tribes\add*, the \add ≈Israelis¦108562\add* gave¦108559 Yehoshua¦108564 (Nun's¦108567 son¦108565) his \add own\add* inheritance¦108563 among¦108568 them¦108568.
\p
\v 50 \add ≈Following Yahweh's¦108573 instructions to¦108575 give¦108574 Yehoshua whatever\add* city he asked¦108580 for¦108580, he was given Timnat¦108583-Serah¦108585 in the¦108586 hill¦108586 country¦108586 of¦108586 Efrayim¦108587 and he built¦108588 \add up\add* that¦108579 city and lived¦108592 in it¦108593.
\p
\v 51 Those were the allotments that¦108597 Eleazar¦108599 the priest¦108600 and Yehoshua¦108602 (Nun's¦108605 son¦108603) gave¦108598 to¦108616 the \add ≈leaders\add* of the Israeli¦108611 tribes¦108608 as¦108598 their inheritances¦108596. It was done by¦108613 throwing dice there in Shiloh¦108615 in front¦108616 of Yahweh¦108617 at¦108613 the opening of the sacred¦108619 tent¦108619, and so the land¦108625 division was completed.
\c 20
\s1 The refuge cities
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge; Cities of refuge; The Cities of Refuge
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦108629 told Yehoshua¦108632,\x + \xo 20:1-9: \xt Num 35:9-34; Deu 4:41-43; 19:1-13.\x*
\v 2 “Tell the¦108638 Israelis¦108639 to select some cities¦108645 that¦108647 people¦108638 can flee to in¦108651 order to be safe, just as I¦108649 instructed you through Mosheh¦108653,
\v 3 so that¦108658 if \add ≈someone accidentally¦108661 kills someone else\add*, they¦108665 can escape there¦108656 and¦108665 be¦108665 safe \add ≈from¦108668 the¦108668 dead person's¦108660 family\add*.
\v 4 When¦108671 \add @that¦108688 person\add* flees¦108671 to one¦108674 of¦108676 these¦108677 cities¦108676, \add they must\add* stand¦108678 at¦108683 the city gate¦108680 and tell the elders¦108684 there what happened. Then¦108671 they should bring \add @the person\add* into the city and give¦108696 \add ≈them¦108701 a place¦108699 there to live in¦108683\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈Now\add* if¦108715 a relative of the deceased comes to¦108727 avenge¦108705 the death, \add @the city elders¦108710\add* won't¦108708 hand¦108714 over the killer¦108713 because \add ≈the death was¦108725 accidental and¦108703 didn't¦108708 happen because of hate¦108725 or premeditation\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦108731 then that person\add* must stay in the city until they're brought before¦108738 \add ≈the panel of judges¦108740\add*. \add If they decide that the death wasn't deliberate,\add* the person must remain in that city until the death of the high priest¦108744, then they can \add freely\add* return¦108752 to¦108755 their own city and¦108731 own home.”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So¦108769\add* \add @the Israelis¦108769\add* chose Kedesh¦108772 (in the Galilee¦108773 region in the hill country of Naftali¦108775) and Shekem¦108778 (in the hill country of Efrayim¦108780) and Kiriat¦108783-Arba¦108784 (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦108786, in the hill country of Yehudah¦108788).
\v 8 On¦108792 the other¦108790 side¦108790 of the Yordan¦108791 \add river\add*, they¦108794 chose Betser¦108797 (in the wilderness¦108798 on¦108798 the plateau¦108799 from the tribe of Reuben¦108801), Ramot¦108804 (in the Gilead¦108805 from the tribe of Gad¦108808), and¦108790 Golan¦108811 (in the Bashan¦108813 from the tribe of Menashsheh¦108815).
\v 9 Those were¦108818 the appointed¦108820 cities¦108819 for¦108825 \add ≈both Israelis¦108824 and foreigners living among¦108827\add* them¦108827, so that¦108826 anyone¦108832 who¦108832 accidentally¦108835 killed someone¦108832 could flee¦108828 there¦108829 and \add ≈be safe from being avenged¦108839 by¦108838 the deceased's relatives\add* until¦108841 \add ≈they¦108818 could receive a proper trial\add*.
\c 21
\s1 The allocation to Levi's descendants
\rem /s1 Towns for the Levites; The Cities of the Levites; Cities Allotted to the Levites; The Towns Given to the Levites
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then the \add ≈leaders\add* of¦108849 the Levites¦108851 went to Eleazar¦108854 the priest¦108855 and to Yehoshua¦108858 (Nun's¦108861 son¦108859) and to the \add ≈Israeli¦108868 elders\add*\x + \xo 21:2: \xt Num 35:1-8.\x*
\v 2 at¦108878 Shiloh¦108872 (in the¦108878 Canaan¦108874 region¦108873) and¦108870 told¦108877 them¦108871, “Yahweh¦108876 said¦108870 \add ≈through\add* Mosheh¦108880 \add ≈that we should be given¦108881 cities¦108884 to¦108875 live¦108885 in, along with¦108878 their¦108886 surrounding fields\add* for¦108887 our¦108887 livestock¦108887.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦108889 the Israeli¦108892\add* \add leaders\add* gave¦108889 these¦108902 cities¦108901 and¦108889 the fields around them to¦108893 the Levites¦108893 for their¦108905 inheritance¦108894 \add ≈as Yahweh¦108898 had instructed\add*:
\p
\v 4 The¦108908 first draw went¦108907 to¦108912 those of the Kohat clans¦108909 \add who were\add* descendants¦108912 of Aharon¦108913 the priest¦108914 (from¦108918 the Levites¦108917). They were allocated thirteen cities¦108925 in¦108924 the regions occupied by¦108924 Yehudah¦108919, Shimeon, and¦108907 Benyamin¦108923.
\v 5 The¦108930 remaining¦108932 Kohat¦108931 \add ≈clans¦108933\add* were \add allocated\add* ten¦108945 cities¦108944 in¦108943 the regions occupied by¦108943 Efrayim¦108936, Dan¦108939, and¦108940 the Menashsheh¦108942 half-tribe.
\p
\v 6 The¦108948 Gereshon¦108949 \add ≈clans¦108950\add* were \add allocated\add* thirteen cities¦108964 in the regions occupied by Yissakar¦108953, Asher¦108956, Naftali¦108958, and¦108954 by the Menashsheh¦108961 half-tribe in the Bashan¦108962 region.
\p
\v 7 The¦108969 Merari¦108970 clans¦108971 were \add allocated\add* twelve cities¦108979 in the¦108972 regions occupied by Reuben¦108973, Gad¦108976, and¦108977 Zebulun¦108978.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦108983 the Israeli¦108986 leaders\add* gave¦108983 those¦108991 cities¦108990 and¦108983 their¦108994 surrounding fields to¦108987 the Levites¦108987, just¦108995 as¦108995 Yahweh¦108997 had¦108996 instructed¦108996 \add ≈through\add* Mosheh¦109000.
\p
\v 9 These¦109013 are the names¦109018 of¦109005 the cities¦109012 \add ≈allocated by the Israeli leaders (from¦109008 the regions occupied by\add* Yehudah¦109007 and¦109004 Shimeon¦109010)
\v 10 that were given to¦109021 the Levite¦109026 Kohat clans¦109023 since \add ≈they were selected first¦109031 in the draw\add*:
\v 11 Kiriat¦109037-Arba and¦109045 the surrounding¦109048 fields (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦109042—Arba was¦109042 the father¦109039 of¦109043 Anak¦109040) in¦109043 Yehudah's¦109044 hill¦109043 country¦109043
\v 12 (although the¦109052 surrounding countryside and¦109054 villages¦109056 had already been given¦109057 to¦109058 Yefunneh's¦109061 son¦109059 Caleb¦109058).
\v 13 \add ≈So\add* Hebron¦109077 was given¦109069 to¦109065 the descendants¦109065 of¦109065 Aharon¦109067 the priest¦109068 and¦109078 assigned as a refuge¦109073 city¦109072 (for anyone who \add accidentally\add* kills someone) along with the surrounding fields, along with Libnah¦109083,
\v 14 Yattir¦109090, Eshtemoa¦109096,
\v 15 Holon¦109103, Debir¦109109,
\v 16 Ain¦109116, Yuttah, and Beyt¦109128-Shemesh¦109129, all with¦109135 their surrounding fields—\add a total of\add* nine¦109134 cities¦109133 from¦109135 within Yehudah and Shimeon's \add territories\add*.
\v 17 From¦109141 Benyamin's¦109142 \add territories\add*, \add the Israeli leaders\add* \add ≈assigned\add* Gibeon¦109145, Geba¦109151,
\v 18 Anatot¦109158, and Almon¦109164—four¦109169 cities¦109168 and their surrounding fields.
\v 19 \add Thus\add* the descendants¦109174 of¦109173 Aharon¦109176 the priests¦109177 \add received\add* thirteen cities¦109181 with their¦109182 surrounding fields.
\p
\v 20 The¦109192 \add other\add* Levite¦109189 Kohat¦109188 clans¦109185 were¦109193 allocated cities¦109194 from¦109191 \add ≈within Efrayim's¦109197 territory\add*:
\v 21 Shekem¦109208 (which was assigned as a refuge¦109204 city¦109203 for¦109200 anyone who \add accidentally\add* kills someone), Gezer¦109216,
\v 22 Kibzaim¦109223, and¦109221 Beyt¦109229-Horon¦109230—four¦109235 cities¦109234 with their surrounding fields.
\v 23 From¦109238 Dan's¦109240 \add territory\add*, they were allocated Elteke¦109243, Gibbeton¦109249,
\v 24 Ayyalon¦109256, and¦109257 Gat¦109262-Rimmon¦109264—four¦109269 cities¦109268 with their surrounding fields.
\v 25 From¦109272 the¦109273 Menashsheh¦109274 half-tribe's \add territory\add*, they were allocated Taanak¦109277 and¦109272 Gat¦109283-Rimmon¦109285—two¦109290 cities¦109289 with their surrounding fields.
\v 26 \add Thus\add* the¦109294 \add other\add* Levite Kohat¦109300 clans¦109297 \add received\add* ten¦109295 cities¦109294 with their¦109296 surrounding fields.
\p
\v 27 The¦109304 Levite¦109307 Gereshon¦109305 clans¦109306 were allocated cities from¦109306 \add ≈within the Menashsheh¦109310 half-tribe's territory\add*: Golan¦109318 in¦109320 the Bashan¦109320 (which was assigned as a refuge¦109314 city¦109313 for anyone¦109306 who \add accidentally\add* kills someone) and¦109321 Be'eshtarah¦109326—two¦109331 cities with¦109320 their surrounding fields.
\v 28 From¦109334 Yissakar's¦109335 \add territory\add*, they were allocated Kishyon¦109338, Daberat¦109344,
\v 29 Yarmut¦109351, and¦109352 Eyn¦109357-Gannim¦109358—four¦109363 cities¦109362 with their surrounding fields.
\v 30 From¦109366 Asher's¦109367 \add territory\add*, they were allocated Mishal¦109370, Abdon¦109376,
\v 31 Helkat¦109383, and¦109384 Rehob¦109389—four¦109394 cities¦109393 with their surrounding fields.
\v 32 From¦109397 Naftali's¦109398 \add territory\add*, they were allocated Kedesh¦109407 in¦109408 the¦109397 Galilee¦109408 (which was assigned as a refuge¦109403 city¦109401 for anyone who \add accidentally\add* kills someone), Hammot¦109414-Dor¦109415, and¦109409 Kartan¦109421—three¦109426 cities¦109425 with¦109408 their surrounding fields.
\v 33 \add Thus\add* the¦109430 Levite Gereshon clan¦109432 \add received\add* thirteen cities¦109430 with their¦109432 surrounding fields.
\p
\v 34 The¦109440 remaining¦109445 Levite¦109444 Merari¦109443 clans¦109440 were allocated cities from¦109446 \add ≈within Zebulun's¦109448 territory\add*: Yokneam¦109451, Kartah¦109457,
\v 35 Dimnah¦109464, and¦109465 Nahalal¦109470—four¦109475 cities¦109474 with their surrounding fields.
\v 36 From¦109477 Reuben's¦109478 \add territory\add*, they were allocated Bezer¦109481, Yahaz¦109487,
\v 37 Kedemot¦109494, and¦109495 Mephaat¦109500—four¦109505 cities¦109504 with their surrounding fields.
\v 38 From¦109508 Gad's¦109510 \add territory\add*, they were allocated Ramot¦109518 in¦109519 the¦109508 Gilead¦109519 (which was assigned as a refuge¦109514 city¦109513 for anyone who \add accidentally\add* kills someone), Mahanaim¦109525,
\v 39 Heshbon¦109532, and¦109533 Yazer¦109538—four¦109545 cities¦109544 with their surrounding fields.
\v 40 \add Thus\add* the Levite¦109555 Merari¦109551 clan¦109552 \add received\add* twelve cities¦109549 in the draw, along with their¦109552 surrounding fields.
\p
\v 41 \add So\add* altogether the Levites¦109564 received forty-eight¦109571 cities¦109563 and¦109572 their¦109573 surrounding fields from with the territories of¦109569 the \add ≈other tribes\add*—
\v 42 each¦109583 of¦109580 those¦109577 cities¦109578 had fields around¦109581 them \add for their livestock to graze on\add*.
\s1 The Israelis move into the regions
\rem /s1 Israel Takes Possession of the Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 43 \add ≈Thus\add* Yahweh¦109590 gave¦109589 \add ≈the Israelis¦109591\add* all¦109594 the land¦109596 that¦109597 he'd promised¦109598 their¦109600 ancestors¦109600 would be given and \add so the people\add* \add ≈moved into those regions\add* and lived¦109602 there.
\v 44 Yahweh gave¦109605 them \add ≈peace\add* as he'd promised¦109612 their ancestors¦109613—none of¦109618 their enemies could stand¦109616 against them \add ≈because¦109607 Yahweh helped¦109607 them defeat¦109607 any¦109607 enemies\add*.
\v 45 \add ≈Yahweh¦109640 kept every¦109645 promise¦109635 that¦109637 he'd made to¦109641 the¦109643 Israelis¦109644—it all¦109634 happened just like he'd said\add*.
\c 22
\s1 The eastern tribes return home
\rem /s1 The Eastern Tribes Return to Their Territory; Eastern Tribes Return Home; Joshua Sends the Eastern Tribes Home; The Eastern Tribes Return Home
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then¦109649 Yehoshua¦109651 \add ≈summoned¦109650\add* the tribes¦109655 of¦109654 Reuben and Gad, and the Menashsheh¦109656 half-tribe
\v 2 and¦109671 told them¦109659, “You yourselves have¦109661 obeyed¦109671 everything that Yahweh's¦109670 servant¦109669 Mosheh¦109668 instructed¦109666 you to¦109672 do. In addition¦109658, you've all¦109673 followed everything that I¦109676 told you.\x + \xo 22:2: \xt Num 32:20-32; Josh 1:12-15.\x*
\v 3 You've all \add ^supported\add* your \add ≈fellow tribes\add* all this¦109690 time¦109686 and¦109691 fulfilled what your god¦109697 Yahweh¦109696 \add ≈requested of¦109694 you¦109681 all\add*,
\v 4 and¦109699 now \add *he\add* has¦109700 enabled \add ≈these other tribes\add* to rest¦109700 \add from battle\add* just¦109704 like he told them¦109706 he would. \add ≈So¦109699\add* now, you all may go¦109709 back to your¦109715 homes that¦109716 Yahweh's¦109701 servant¦109721 Mosheh¦109720 gave¦109718 you on¦109723 the \add ≈other\add* side¦109723 of¦109723 the river.
\v 5 Only¦109726 do¦109730 take¦109728 care¦109728 to \add continue to\add* obey the instructions and the law¦109736 that¦109737 Yahweh's¦109743 servant¦109741 Mosheh¦109740 gave you: to love¦109744 your god¦109748 Yahweh, to \add ≈follow him and his¦109754 instructions\add*, to \add ≈stay close to him\add*, and to serve¦109758 him with all¦109759 your hearts¦109761 and your \add inner\add* selves.”
\v 6 Then¦109766 Yehoshua¦109767 blessed¦109766 them and¦109766 sent¦109768 them on their way to return to their \add ≈homes\add*.
\v 7 (Mosheh¦109780 had given the Bashan¦109781 to the half of the Menashsheh¦109778 half-tribe, and¦109782 Yehoshua¦109784 had given \add land\add* on¦109781 the \add ≈western\add* side¦109788 of the Yordan¦109791 to the other¦109788 half.) \add When\add* he'd blessed¦109800 them¦109800
\v 8 he'd said¦109802, “Go back to¦109803 your \add ≈homes\add* with many¦109820 riches¦109805: plenty of livestock¦109811, and with silver¦109815, gold¦109816, bronze¦109817, and iron¦109818, and with lots of clothing¦109819. Share the¦109823 plunder from your enemies¦109825 with \add ≈those¦109803 who¦109803 remained¦109803 behind¦109803\add*.”
\v 9 So¦109845 \add ≈the warriors from¦109843 the tribes¦109841 of\add* Reuven¦109835, Gad¦109838, and the Menashsheh¦109842 half-tribe left the \add ≈others\add* there at¦109863 Shiloh¦109846 in the Canaan¦109850 region¦109848, and went¦109832 back to¦109856 their¦109859 own¦109859 land¦109858 in Gilead¦109855 \add across the river\add* which¦109860 they¦109861 had¦109861 taken for themselves with¦109863 the agreement of Yahweh¦109867 given through Mosheh¦109870.
\s1 The altar by the Yordan
\rem /s1 A Memorial Altar East of the Jordan; The Altar by the Jordan; The Eastern Tribes Build a Memorial
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 \add ≈The¦109876 warriors from the tribes¦109888 of¦109881\add* Reuven¦109883, Gad¦109886, and the Menashsheh¦109889 half-tribe arrived¦109872 at¦109892 the Yordan¦109894 river (still on the Canaan¦109879 side) and they¦109872 built¦109880 a very large¦109896 and noticeable altar¦109891 there¦109890 \add before crossing over to go home\add*.
\v 11 \add When\add* the \add other\add* \add ≈Israelis¦109902\add* heard¦109899 \add about it\add*, they¦109905 said¦109903, “Look, the men \add ≈from the tribes¦109913 of¦109911\add* Reuven¦109908, Gad¦109911, and¦109899 the Menashsheh¦109914 half-tribe have¦109905 built¦109905 the altar¦109917 at the \add ≈entrance to¦109918 this\add* Canaan¦109922 region¦109921 down at the Yordan¦109926 on \add *our\add* side¦109929.”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈Hearing that, those from the western side of¦109934 the Yordan assembled¦109936 at Shiloh¦109943 to go¦109944 to battle¦109946 with the two and¦109936 a half tribes on¦109945 the eastern side\add*.
\v 13 \add Meanwhile\add*, they¦109949 sent¦109949 the priest¦109979 Finehas¦109975 (Eleazar's¦109978 son¦109976) \add across\add* into the Gilead¦109972 region¦109971 \add to talk\add* with \add the leaders from\add* the tribes¦109966 of¦109960 Reuben¦109957, Gad¦109962, and¦109963 the Menashsheh¦109968 half-tribe.
\v 14 \add @Finehas¦109997\add* took ten¦109981 leaders with¦109983 him—important leaders from each¦109990 of¦109991 the Israeli¦109991 tribes¦109991 \add from the western side\add*.
\v 15 They \add crossed over\add* to the Gilead¦110022 region¦110021 to talk¦110023 to \add the leaders from\add* the tribes¦110016 of¦110016 Reuben¦110007, Gad¦110012, and¦110002 the Menashsheh¦110018 half-tribe. They said¦110023,
\v 16 “Yahweh's¦110032 people are¦110035 \add ≈asking\add*, ‘What's¦110033 this¦110036 unfaithfulness¦110035 that¦110037 you all¦110029 have¦110038 done unfaithfully¦110038 against Yisrael's¦110040 god¦110039—turning¦110041 away from¦110043 Yahweh when¦110045 you built¦110045 an¦110047 altar¦110047 for¦110046 yourselves¦110045 today in¦110039 rebellion¦110048 against Yahweh?\x + \xo 22:16: \xt Deu 12:13-14.\x*
\v 17 Wasn't \add ≈our disobedience at¦110069 Peor¦110058\add*\x + \xo 22:17: \xt Num 25:1-9.\x* \add ≈bad enough¦110052 for¦110054 you\add*? We¦110062 haven't \add ≈gotten over it¦110063\add* to¦110054 this¦110066 day¦110065. Plus there was¦110067 a \add ≈deadly disease\add* among¦110069 Yahweh's¦110070 people.
